WEBVTT

01:18.560 --> 01:20.341
<i>Dude, don't just sit there. Come on!</i>

01:20.342 --> 01:21.715
<i>The show's started. Come, come!</i>

01:21.716 --> 01:23.777
<i>- Oh, get lost, man!
- Varun... Varun Thambi, just come!</i>

01:23.778 --> 01:25.527
<i>What, man! What's there to see?</i>

01:25.528 --> 01:26.746
<i>Dude, it's the Metal!</i>

01:26.747 --> 01:28.509
<i>It's a killer Metal show, bro!</i>

01:28.510 --> 01:30.435
<i>I don't care! Metal, my foot!</i>

01:30.436 --> 01:32.036
<i>Stop fussing and just come, bro.</i>

01:32.037 --> 01:33.973
<i>I'm telling you, bro... Metal...</i>

01:33.974 --> 01:35.261
<i>He's been like this since first year.</i>

01:35.262 --> 01:37.310
<i>First of all, you know what?
Sumesh just called.</i>

01:37.311 --> 01:39.958
<i>They can't even get in.
The grills are locked.</i>

01:39.959 --> 01:42.286
<i>They'll open it in a bit.</i>

01:42.287 --> 01:44.168
<i>Dude, Joppan will fix it.</i>

01:44.169 --> 01:46.333
<i>I'm not watching from outside
like an idiot.</i>

01:46.427 --> 01:49.192
<i>Wait, wait.
Let's watch it for ten minutes and...</i>

01:49.555 --> 01:55.147
<i>Nearly three decades
before this age of relentless speed,</i>

01:55.148 --> 01:59.374
<i>there was a golden era.</i>

01:59.610 --> 02:00.798
Back then...

02:00.799 --> 02:02.491
when I was doing my Pre-Degree...

02:06.258 --> 02:07.438
That was...

02:07.439 --> 02:09.649
the golden era of our college.

02:09.811 --> 02:11.404
- What the hell?!
- But...

02:11.569 --> 02:14.236
the dance event they conducted then

02:14.237 --> 02:19.233
was unfortunately... below average,

02:19.733 --> 02:22.109
the enjoyment was incredibly scarce.

02:22.520 --> 02:23.535
Who the hell is that?

02:23.536 --> 02:25.883
But today, things are different.

02:27.384 --> 02:33.818
This choir group called
'Iron Foxes Heavy Metal'...

02:34.690 --> 02:35.956
Choir group?!

02:36.828 --> 02:37.844
What the heck, man?!

02:49.423 --> 02:51.213
Hey Sambhu,
tell them to open the gates.

02:51.214 --> 02:53.156
The students outside are going wild.

02:53.514 --> 02:55.484
Whatever I do,
the principal has to agree first.

02:55.485 --> 02:56.735
Let's wait till Joppan gets here.

02:56.736 --> 02:58.895
Damn, where is he?!

02:59.180 --> 03:01.278
That's because
they didn't send the article, right?

03:01.279 --> 03:02.836
We've almost reached, don't worry.

03:02.837 --> 03:04.157
One sec. Papa's calling.

03:04.827 --> 03:06.009
Hello?

03:06.173 --> 03:08.398
How's it going?
Did you collect the prints from the press?

03:08.399 --> 03:11.909
No, Joppan's dad said
he'd pick up the magazine copies.

03:12.890 --> 03:15.467
This last-minute panic
is totally my daughter's trademark.

03:15.468 --> 03:17.976
I didn't delay it on purpose, Papa.

03:18.143 --> 03:20.129
That haiku poem
from the Mechanical department,

03:20.130 --> 03:22.443
“The guys who loved iron more than women.”

03:22.444 --> 03:23.818
came in only last night.

03:24.393 --> 03:26.712
If I leave that out,
those guys will burn me alive.

03:28.061 --> 03:30.048
Anyway, hope the event's a huge hit.

03:30.864 --> 03:31.995
Rock the speech, okay?

03:31.996 --> 03:33.226
Okay, Papa.

03:33.227 --> 03:34.364
Is Joppan with you?

03:34.365 --> 03:35.437
<i>Yeah.</i>

03:35.438 --> 03:37.023
Give him my regards.

03:39.763 --> 03:40.989
What did he say?

03:41.340 --> 03:43.400
Told me to pass on his regards to you!

03:50.947 --> 03:52.227
Ah, there they are.

03:53.732 --> 03:54.869
Didn't those guys come?

03:54.870 --> 03:56.843
- I hope I don't screw up the speech!
- You won't!

03:56.844 --> 03:59.428
Dear, I could only print 20 copies.

03:59.429 --> 04:00.377
That's enough.

04:00.378 --> 04:03.838
Just need a few copies for the chief guest
and those on stage after the launch.

04:04.052 --> 04:05.179
Here, take this.

04:08.708 --> 04:09.981
Aren't you coming in, Dad?

04:10.261 --> 04:11.989
No, I still haven't closed the shop.

04:11.990 --> 04:13.207
- You go ahead.
- Okay.

04:13.208 --> 04:15.478
Could you tell Samkutty
the event's about to start?

04:15.593 --> 04:18.480
He heard the old flagpole at
Mamalassery temple has iridium in it,

04:18.481 --> 04:20.719
so he went there with his gang
to scrape it off.

04:21.217 --> 04:23.034
Said he'll return only as a millionaire.

04:23.035 --> 04:24.407
You just go do your work.

04:24.609 --> 04:25.748
Alright then.

04:25.749 --> 04:26.801
So, are we getting something?

04:26.802 --> 04:28.434
Let the program end,
we'll arrange something.

04:28.435 --> 04:29.696
- Make sure you do.
- Let's go.

04:29.697 --> 04:31.612
You better be there
for the publishing ceremony, okay?

04:31.613 --> 04:33.791
I need your opinion
on my editorial note.

04:33.792 --> 04:35.324
Okay, I will. Wait a sec.

04:35.325 --> 04:36.503
Hey, hold this.

04:37.064 --> 04:38.133
Take it.

04:38.134 --> 04:39.192
Where were you?

04:39.193 --> 04:40.916
Bro, massive block at Palayam!

04:40.917 --> 04:41.992
Perfect!

04:42.113 --> 04:43.210
Everything okay here?

04:43.211 --> 04:45.556
Those first-years are creating chaos there.

04:45.557 --> 04:46.730
There's space in the Parents' Area.

04:46.731 --> 04:48.862
But that damn Lovely Madam
won't let us open the gate.

04:48.863 --> 04:50.553
Damn, we collected money from them too!

04:50.554 --> 04:51.672
Exactly!

04:52.031 --> 04:53.807
- I'll handle it.
- What are you gonna do?

04:54.311 --> 04:55.908
We just need the key to open it, right?

04:55.909 --> 04:57.693
Who needs permission?
- Okay then.

04:57.694 --> 05:00.242
Don’t invite trouble for no reason.
If Lovely Madam finds out, you're dead.

05:00.243 --> 05:01.761
- You hurry up. Fast.
- I'll manage.

05:01.762 --> 05:03.583
- Don't make a scene.
- I won't! I won't!

05:03.704 --> 05:05.891
I won't... drag this out.

05:05.984 --> 05:07.040
Oh, Jesus!

05:07.041 --> 05:08.815
Thank you.

05:28.487 --> 05:29.721
♪ Open them wide! ♪

05:31.467 --> 05:32.815
♪ Open them wide! ♪

05:35.273 --> 05:36.617
♪ Open them wide! ♪

05:38.442 --> 05:39.723
♪ Open them wide! ♪

05:44.605 --> 05:47.650
♪ Afraid, afraid, always afraid ♪

05:47.651 --> 05:50.603
♪ Neither truly living, nor truly dying ♪

05:50.604 --> 05:53.416
♪ Afraid, afraid, always afraid ♪

05:53.620 --> 05:56.260
♪ Neither truly living, nor truly dying ♪

05:56.261 --> 05:58.939
♪ Killed them, killed them! ♪

05:58.940 --> 06:02.354
♪ Once again, Killed them, killed them! ♪

06:02.620 --> 06:04.565
♪ We murdered every single doubt ♪

06:04.665 --> 06:07.118
The magazine launch is happening
just before the final song.

06:07.497 --> 06:08.714
And you're telling me this now?

06:08.715 --> 06:10.888
There was a last-minute mix-up.

06:11.311 --> 06:12.405
Where's Joppan?

06:12.722 --> 06:14.518
♪ Brimming with freedom, freedom again! ♪

06:14.519 --> 06:16.110
Joppan went to open the gate.

06:16.261 --> 06:17.501
Go tell him.

06:17.502 --> 06:18.776
♪ Open them wide! ♪

06:18.777 --> 06:20.631
♪ Brimming with freedom ♪

06:20.632 --> 06:21.746
♪ Open them wide! ♪

06:21.747 --> 06:23.566
♪ Brimming with freedom ♪

06:23.567 --> 06:24.714
♪ Open them wide! ♪

06:24.715 --> 06:26.287
♪ Brimming with freedom ♪

06:26.288 --> 06:27.706
♪ Open them wide! ♪

06:29.667 --> 06:31.480
No, no! Don't push!

06:31.614 --> 06:33.355
♪ Open them wide! ♪

06:33.356 --> 06:35.254
♪ Open your mind, open it wide! ♪

06:35.255 --> 06:36.332
♪ Open them wide! ♪

06:36.333 --> 06:38.316
♪ Unleash your rhythm, let it out! ♪

06:38.317 --> 06:39.394
♪ Open them wide! ♪

06:39.395 --> 06:41.229
♪ Broaden your vision, open it wide! ♪

06:53.222 --> 06:54.589
♪ Brimming with freedom ♪

06:56.206 --> 06:57.448
♪ Brimming with freedom ♪

06:59.245 --> 07:00.519
♪ Brimming with freedom ♪

07:02.245 --> 07:03.745
♪ Brimming with freedom ♪

07:05.237 --> 07:06.628
♪ Open them wide! ♪

07:08.230 --> 07:09.581
♪ Open them wide! ♪

07:11.214 --> 07:12.464
♪ Open them wide! ♪

07:14.237 --> 07:15.605
♪ Open them wide! ♪

07:17.245 --> 07:18.636
♪ Open them wide! ♪

07:20.222 --> 07:21.519
♪ Open them wide! ♪

07:23.261 --> 07:24.667
♪ Open them wide! ♪

07:26.151 --> 07:27.800
♪ Open them wide! ♪

07:35.032 --> 07:36.523
Merin...
Move aside, you!

07:38.633 --> 07:39.883
Move, I said!

07:59.242 --> 08:00.502
Merin!

08:03.874 --> 08:05.641
Hey, Sambhu!

08:08.280 --> 08:09.846
Come on, man!

08:14.234 --> 08:15.594
Merin!

08:24.068 --> 08:26.241
<i>Merin, Chaitra, and Akhil
are the three students</i>

08:26.242 --> 08:28.252
<i>who lost their lives
in yesterday's stampede.</i>

08:28.253 --> 08:30.693
<i>An expert committee has been appointed...</i>

09:01.550 --> 09:02.616
<i>♪ What's up? ♪</i>

09:02.617 --> 09:03.676
<i>♪ Queue up ♪</i>

09:03.677 --> 09:04.762
<i>♪ Line up ♪</i>

09:04.763 --> 09:05.823
<i>♪ Back up ♪</i>

09:05.824 --> 09:06.899
<i>♪ Right speck ♪</i>

09:06.900 --> 09:07.943
<i>♪ New tech ♪</i>

09:07.944 --> 09:09.021
<i>♪ Team Mech ♪</i>

09:09.022 --> 09:14.800
<i>♪ Vibe check! ♪</i>

09:14.801 --> 09:15.947
Oh, so you can dance too?

09:16.152 --> 09:17.232
Yes, ma'am.

09:18.227 --> 09:20.113
He’s got this poetry bug too.

09:21.102 --> 09:22.474
Alpha male... alpha male...

09:22.584 --> 09:23.632
What?

09:23.633 --> 09:25.856
Madam, I've got a few alpha male traits.

09:29.125 --> 09:30.152
Ouch!

09:32.416 --> 09:33.460
Are they all here?

09:33.461 --> 09:34.553
Not really.

09:34.554 --> 09:36.971
One guy from the church scholarship list
hasn’t arrived yet.

09:36.972 --> 09:37.969
Who's that?

09:37.970 --> 09:39.004
God knows!

09:39.632 --> 09:41.919
<i>My strength: crisis management.</i>

09:42.117 --> 09:44.270
<i>Weakness: over-hardworking.</i>

09:44.405 --> 09:46.810
<i>Total dedication freak.
Probably doesn't even sleep.</i>

09:46.946 --> 09:48.038
Who's this clown?

09:48.039 --> 09:49.048
Only God knows.

10:02.819 --> 10:05.291
Come, let's go there.
It's the next block.

10:05.292 --> 10:07.612
Brother had crazy fan following here,
right Dad?

10:09.721 --> 10:10.813
Come.

10:13.527 --> 10:16.180
Son, I'm asking you one last time.

10:16.520 --> 10:18.040
Are you sure about this?

10:18.134 --> 10:19.914
Everyone's doing engineering these days.

10:20.147 --> 10:22.333
In a few years, the demand will crash.

10:23.065 --> 10:25.156
Dad, don't talk without vision.

10:25.259 --> 10:27.517
How will people survive
without bridges and buildings?

10:27.695 --> 10:31.348
And Dad, you know
my biggest strength is crisis management.

10:31.711 --> 10:33.158
Engineering is perfect for that.

10:33.159 --> 10:34.423
Haven't you watched 3 Idiots?

10:34.424 --> 10:35.552
No.

10:35.893 --> 10:36.967
Exactly my point!

10:39.916 --> 10:42.406
- You're Joseph's brother, right?
- Yes, sir.

10:42.407 --> 10:43.742
Where's Joseph these days?

10:43.949 --> 10:46.180
He's in Thoothukudi.
Working at a company there.

10:47.677 --> 10:49.690
I was coordinating that case back then.

10:49.830 --> 10:51.403
Couldn't reach him after that.

10:51.589 --> 10:52.809
Okay, leave it.

10:53.209 --> 10:55.963
Wait, Joseph Kutty,
you're two years behind.

10:56.472 --> 10:58.023
Samkutty. I'm Samkutty.

10:58.024 --> 10:59.390
Sorry, Samkutty. What happened?

10:59.391 --> 11:00.980
Sir, I took a repeat for IIT.

11:00.981 --> 11:02.060
Really? Then?

11:02.061 --> 11:04.253
While repeating, I realised...

11:04.254 --> 11:07.268
when a prestigious college like BCET
is right next door...

11:07.588 --> 11:09.374
where curiosity meets wisdom.

11:10.743 --> 11:13.007
And my brother studied here too.

11:15.104 --> 11:17.218
This admission is through
the church scholarship.

11:17.428 --> 11:20.785
If you fail even one subject
or your attendance drops,

11:20.786 --> 11:22.776
- the scholarship will get revoked.
- Yeah, I know.

11:22.777 --> 11:24.849
Then your dad will have to pay the fees.

11:24.850 --> 11:25.863
He'll pay.

11:25.864 --> 11:26.888
Sir, your tea.

11:29.649 --> 11:30.803
So tell me, Samkutty.

11:30.804 --> 11:33.779
Why did you choose Civil Engineering?

11:37.703 --> 11:39.302
Sir, when workers came

11:39.389 --> 11:41.217
to build our house back then...

11:41.966 --> 11:44.469
they'd spread sand on the ground like this.

11:45.149 --> 11:47.428
Then they'd pour cement over it

11:47.429 --> 11:49.233
and mix it together.

11:50.334 --> 11:53.279
Once the color became nice and even...

11:53.766 --> 11:55.841
they'd add gravel on top

11:55.842 --> 11:57.623
and mix everything together.

11:58.461 --> 12:00.294
Then they'd dig a hole right in the middle,

12:00.687 --> 12:02.300
and pour water into it.

12:02.783 --> 12:06.490
After that, they'd take a spade
and keep mixing everything.

12:07.729 --> 12:09.218
Mixing and mixing...

12:09.936 --> 12:11.007
Sir...

12:11.008 --> 12:12.756
when it turns all mushy and gooey,

12:12.912 --> 12:14.819
you just feel like eating it!

12:15.303 --> 12:16.576
That's when I realised, sir,

12:16.670 --> 12:18.363
there's a Civil Engineer living inside me.

12:22.889 --> 12:24.813
You could've sent him as a mason's helper.

12:24.814 --> 12:26.719
Why take such a huge risk at this age?

12:26.807 --> 12:28.003
That would've been better.

12:28.802 --> 12:29.916
Madam...

12:30.013 --> 12:32.862
that church scholarship guy
looks like a total idiot.

12:33.122 --> 12:35.322
He's our Joseph's younger brother.

12:35.679 --> 12:37.952
It's a special recommendation
directly from the Bishop.

12:37.953 --> 12:39.192
Just give him admission.

12:39.490 --> 12:41.430
Besides, Joseph was like this too at first.

12:41.431 --> 12:42.727
He'll learn eventually.

12:43.292 --> 12:44.805
Guess it runs in their genes.

12:45.118 --> 12:47.144
<i>♪ If you know you know ♪</i>

12:48.312 --> 12:50.750
Oh! So he’s got
the ‘he’ll learn eventually’ gene, huh?

12:51.176 --> 12:52.788
<i>♪ If you know you know ♪</i>

12:52.789 --> 12:55.166
<i>♪ One stolen glance,
and she got cemented in my heart ♪</i>

12:55.167 --> 12:57.489
<i>♪ One tiny smile,
and she flooded my soul ♪</i>

12:57.618 --> 13:01.471
<i>♪ A love story built
on a solid concrete base ♪</i>

13:01.596 --> 13:04.279
That's the Smithy. I mean, the forge.

13:04.280 --> 13:05.660
Beyond that is the Foundry.

13:05.661 --> 13:07.829
Sir, where do they teach about
concrete and stuff?

13:08.826 --> 13:10.358
Boy, first stand properly on the ground.

13:10.359 --> 13:12.110
When the time comes,
I'll teach you all that.

13:12.111 --> 13:13.816
Where are you from? Huh?

13:13.817 --> 13:14.857
He got embarrassed!

13:16.067 --> 13:17.145
Silly fellow!

13:17.533 --> 13:19.033
<i>♪ If you know you know ♪</i>

13:22.412 --> 13:24.477
Okay, all of you welcome to the campus.

13:24.725 --> 13:27.591
<i>See, the reason you all chose
engineering...</i>

13:27.809 --> 13:28.900
That's Lakshmi.

13:28.901 --> 13:30.959
The other one's Tanvi.
And that's Elizabeth.

13:31.077 --> 13:32.864
I'm Prasanth.
People call me Parashu.

13:33.502 --> 13:35.375
I'm Samkutty.
People call me Samboy.

13:36.625 --> 13:38.329
- What's that girl's name?
- Who? Elizabeth?

13:38.330 --> 13:39.643
Not Elizabeth. The other one.

13:39.890 --> 13:41.243
Swathi R Krishna.

13:41.472 --> 13:43.039
Ramesh Marbles owner’s daughter.

13:44.619 --> 13:45.867
Which department?

13:45.868 --> 13:48.268
<i>♪ You're my only backlog this semester ♪</i>

13:49.081 --> 13:53.928
<i>♪ Just sit with me for half an hour,
You crazy-cute pookie ♪</i>

13:53.929 --> 13:57.017
<i>♪ Too many desires,
My mind's in jet mode now ♪</i>

13:57.018 --> 13:58.230
<i>♪ Tell me... what's the cure? ♪</i>

13:58.231 --> 14:01.075
<i>♪ Your smile turns into songs in my ears ♪</i>

14:02.377 --> 14:04.603
One sec,
I'll hit the washroom and come.

14:04.604 --> 14:05.992
Make it quick.

14:06.613 --> 14:08.481
If it's not here,
it'll be in the other lab.

14:08.705 --> 14:09.952
Murakami?

14:10.845 --> 14:12.924
- Swathi R Krishna?
- Murakami, right?

14:13.246 --> 14:14.260
What?

14:14.726 --> 14:16.547
Norwegian Wood? Murakami?

14:16.766 --> 14:18.392
No, Levi's Original!

14:20.432 --> 14:22.182
- Nice T-shirt.
- Thanks.

14:22.183 --> 14:23.777
- Original!
- Totally original!

14:23.778 --> 14:24.859
Absolute idiot!

14:25.102 --> 14:26.134
Yes!

14:28.773 --> 14:30.198
Murakami. That's what she said.

14:30.199 --> 14:31.218
Oh, damn!

14:31.219 --> 14:33.602
- Isn't he Joseph's younger brother?
- She’s sapiosexual.

14:33.603 --> 14:36.350
A sapiosexual is someone
who feels attracted to people

14:36.351 --> 14:37.617
because of their intelligence.

14:37.618 --> 14:39.493
Steve Jobs, Zuckerberg, Elon--

14:39.494 --> 14:41.464
GS Pradeep, Shashi Tharoor, Maitreyan.

14:41.892 --> 14:44.260
<i>♪ One stolen glance,
and she got cemented in my heart ♪</i>

14:44.261 --> 14:46.548
<i>♪ One tiny smile,
and she flooded my soul ♪</i>

14:46.648 --> 14:50.445
<i>♪ A love story built
on a solid concrete base ♪</i>

14:50.446 --> 14:52.152
<i>♪ Is she for real
or straight out of a movie? ♪</i>

14:52.153 --> 14:53.050
Oops!

14:53.051 --> 14:54.031
Sorry! Sorry!

14:54.032 --> 14:55.750
Ohhh... show!

14:55.751 --> 14:57.551
<i>♪ Is she sigma...
Or an enigma? ♪</i>

14:57.641 --> 14:58.654
Osho!

15:02.133 --> 15:03.153
What's this?

15:06.615 --> 15:07.621
Look!

15:07.971 --> 15:10.707
Man, I don't think she's sapiosexual.

15:11.260 --> 15:13.600
Even Einstein wouldn't impress her.

15:14.683 --> 15:15.876
Will this bloom?

15:20.518 --> 15:21.551
Hey.

15:21.810 --> 15:23.435
That might actually bloom.

15:23.436 --> 15:24.894
Spain has similar ones too.

15:26.086 --> 15:28.146
What now? Go propose to her, bro.

15:28.711 --> 15:30.545
He says he's an Alpha Male.

15:30.764 --> 15:32.036
Need to be a bit careful.

15:32.037 --> 15:33.883
Oh God.
Let that loser turn out to be toxic!

15:35.330 --> 15:37.033
Should I propose today itself?
How about tomorrow?

15:37.034 --> 15:38.214
You said that yesterday too!

15:38.215 --> 15:39.681
If you wait,
that Alpha guy will take her!

15:39.682 --> 15:40.658
No way!

15:40.659 --> 15:43.879
And after proposing, tell her,
‘You’ve got beautiful eyes.’

15:43.986 --> 15:45.099
Come on, say it once.

15:45.984 --> 15:47.333
I’ve got beautiful eyes, right?

15:47.334 --> 15:48.959
Dude! Not your eyes, hers!

15:49.918 --> 15:51.282
Don't confuse me.

15:51.283 --> 15:52.443
I have a master plan.

15:53.416 --> 15:54.450
Listen...

15:55.777 --> 15:56.722
Where are you going?

15:56.723 --> 15:58.827
Avoid cracking lame jokes
while talking. Please.

15:58.828 --> 16:00.091
Go. Make her fall for you.

16:01.271 --> 16:02.351
Hey!

16:04.859 --> 16:06.052
Look who's here!

16:06.574 --> 16:07.947
The goddess of the temple herself?

16:14.812 --> 16:16.007
Parashu...

16:19.690 --> 16:20.910
Hey girl...

16:21.243 --> 16:22.945
Shall I tie the knot

16:22.946 --> 16:24.679
and take you home with me?

16:27.056 --> 16:28.084
Dude...

16:28.085 --> 16:29.694
He’s a total red flag!

16:29.874 --> 16:30.961
Red flag?

16:31.151 --> 16:32.421
I'm not into politics.

16:32.422 --> 16:34.460
- My dad used to be--
- Not that, doofus!

16:34.461 --> 16:35.503
Come on, let's go.

16:38.321 --> 16:39.434
0.7.

16:42.343 --> 16:43.596
Bro, Swathi's coming.

16:46.440 --> 16:48.783
Remember what I told you, right?
Maintain that tough look.

16:48.784 --> 16:50.668
Only the Forbidden Fruit theory
will work now.

16:51.094 --> 16:53.284
- Bro, explain once more.
- It's simple.

16:53.285 --> 16:55.285
Whenever you see her,
act like she doesn't exist.

16:55.286 --> 16:56.506
Then she'll start wondering

16:56.507 --> 16:57.898
why you're ignoring her.

16:58.089 --> 16:59.702
Whenever she comes around...

17:00.261 --> 17:02.731
just stay in full "whatever" mode.

17:02.995 --> 17:04.655
Eventually, she'll come to you herself.

17:04.822 --> 17:06.070
That's FFT.

17:06.071 --> 17:07.158
FTV...

17:07.159 --> 17:09.719
What if I approach her
pretending to be a street photographer--

17:09.720 --> 17:10.862
Bro, have you lost it?

17:11.029 --> 17:12.842
- Just shut up. No need of that.
- Right?

17:17.096 --> 17:18.882
- There's that guy again.
- We're screwed.

17:19.636 --> 17:20.876
Bro, where are you going?

17:25.542 --> 17:26.735
What's this now?

17:26.849 --> 17:28.820
Isn't this the 'whatever' you mentioned?

17:28.821 --> 17:30.030
This attitude works, right?

17:30.031 --> 17:31.186
Yeah, sure. Go ahead.

17:33.904 --> 17:35.744
Everyone, please calm down.

17:36.607 --> 17:37.824
One at a time.

17:37.825 --> 17:39.104
Shanu, what's the issue?

17:39.105 --> 17:41.184
Sir, due to some incident
that happened years ago,

17:41.185 --> 17:43.623
you won't even approve
an inter-department fest.

17:43.624 --> 17:45.141
This college feels like a graveyard now.

17:45.142 --> 17:46.398
Same with Freshers' Day too.

17:46.399 --> 17:47.692
Let me finish. Don't interrupt.

17:47.693 --> 17:50.483
We couldn't even organize
a Freshers' Day for the juniors.

17:50.484 --> 17:52.183
They're all disappointed.

17:52.184 --> 17:55.084
Hey, these are decisions
taken by the governing council.

17:55.575 --> 17:57.340
What governing council, sir...

17:57.341 --> 17:58.560
Listen.

17:58.561 --> 18:01.203
Our college focuses mainly on academics.

18:01.204 --> 18:03.237
The God from the temple is here!

18:03.571 --> 18:05.751
Besides, we have
online essay competitions,

18:06.097 --> 18:07.853
- Sudoku and all that.
- Sudoku?!

18:07.854 --> 18:09.032
Are those even events, sir?

18:09.033 --> 18:10.508
Then what about Arohan Fest?

18:11.570 --> 18:14.664
Nobody should utter the word "Arohan"
inside this campus again.

18:15.146 --> 18:16.278
What nonsense is he saying?

18:16.279 --> 18:19.093
And if you keep bringing it up,

18:19.094 --> 18:22.444
I'll even cancel the Sudoku competition.

18:25.529 --> 18:26.615
Oh, just cancel it!

18:26.616 --> 18:28.606
Anything else regarding the union?

18:28.607 --> 18:30.098
- No sir, that's all.
- Then go to your classes.

18:30.099 --> 18:31.200
If you don't allow us--

18:31.201 --> 18:32.428
Hey, listen!

18:32.773 --> 18:34.187
I'll cut your attendance!

18:34.653 --> 18:37.838
- I'll cut all your attendance. Now go.
- Go to class.

18:37.839 --> 18:39.330
Go to your classes. Move.

18:39.331 --> 18:41.329
What an attitude! Cranky old geezer!

18:41.600 --> 18:43.924
- These seniors are such a joke.
- Silly folks!

18:43.925 --> 18:46.049
Anyone else would've
pulled off the fest by now.

18:46.190 --> 18:48.685
Who here is capable of that?

18:49.052 --> 18:51.005
This is all just the seniors showing off.

18:51.006 --> 18:53.525
Organizing a fest takes real effort.

18:53.526 --> 18:54.586
Capable?

18:59.656 --> 19:01.922
Man, the "Whatever" era is over.

19:02.075 --> 19:03.933
Now begins the "Capability" era.

19:03.934 --> 19:06.854
If I revive the Arohan Fest
that’s been dead for two years,

19:06.855 --> 19:08.322
she'll see my capability.

19:09.565 --> 19:12.176
Besides, my brother was the convener
of the last Arohan Fest.

19:12.177 --> 19:13.837
We've got the legacy already.

19:14.274 --> 19:16.719
Who do you think you are?
Jagannathan from Aaraam Thampuran?

19:17.312 --> 19:18.911
Yes. Jagannathan!

19:19.158 --> 19:21.252
- So, dear Jagannathan...
- Yes, dear?

19:21.253 --> 19:23.920
Your friend Prasanth here
has a total net worth of 114 rupees.

19:24.578 --> 19:26.608
Even if you give me more time,
nothing's changing.

19:26.609 --> 19:28.949
To conduct the fest,
the management has to approve it.

19:29.081 --> 19:31.741
And that approval must land in our hands
like a divine ornament.

19:31.989 --> 19:33.221
Can you pull that off?

19:34.393 --> 19:35.706
Approval?

19:35.861 --> 19:37.448
We'll give the principal an application

19:37.449 --> 19:39.295
so emotional,
he'll cry reading it.

19:39.296 --> 19:40.883
This is a silly crisis.

19:41.351 --> 19:42.366
And I will manage.

19:46.941 --> 19:48.201
Hey, what's behind you?

19:49.265 --> 19:51.083
I asked what's on the back of your head.

19:51.084 --> 19:53.221
Oh! My hair? That’s my style!

19:53.441 --> 19:55.040
Superb style!

19:55.379 --> 19:57.437
- You use conditioner and all?
- Yeah.

19:57.533 --> 19:58.871
- Which one?
- Dove.

19:59.058 --> 20:00.627
- Dove? Daily?
- Twice a week.

20:00.628 --> 20:01.715
Hey, kiddo.

20:03.906 --> 20:05.632
Heard you're quite the fun guy around here.

20:06.471 --> 20:08.326
- Nothing like that, bro.
- Nothing like that?

20:09.068 --> 20:11.034
Just got here and
already running the show?!

20:11.035 --> 20:13.069
Take it easy.
You've still got 3-4 years left here.

20:13.773 --> 20:15.289
Looks like trouble!

20:15.737 --> 20:18.011
Were you the one who submitted
the Arohan Fest request?

20:18.285 --> 20:19.323
Yeah.

20:19.324 --> 20:20.781
- We--
- What the hell is your problem?

20:21.980 --> 20:23.984
- Let me talk. You wanna go first?
- Go ahead.

20:23.985 --> 20:26.350
We weren't just sitting around
doing nothing here.

20:26.439 --> 20:27.653
Because of your dumb request,

20:27.654 --> 20:29.538
the one event we had
is about to get cancelled.

20:29.539 --> 20:31.737
I'm sick of hearing taunts
from students of other colleges.

20:31.738 --> 20:32.852
We're suffering even now

20:32.853 --> 20:35.334
because your brother messed around
and killed 3 people.

20:35.678 --> 20:37.055
Don't drag my brother into this.

20:37.056 --> 20:38.860
Oh, did the kid lose his temper?

20:38.861 --> 20:40.172
Don't try to intimidate me.

20:40.728 --> 20:42.452
I'm trembling already.
Might wet my pants.

20:43.780 --> 20:45.040
You little punk.

20:45.166 --> 20:47.185
If you keep acting smart around here,

20:47.186 --> 20:49.180
you won't even survive a year here.
Got it?

20:50.131 --> 20:51.203
Where's your ID tag?

20:51.204 --> 20:52.365
Where's the tag?

20:56.651 --> 20:57.684
Scared now?

20:58.867 --> 20:59.921
Don't you want to study?

21:00.267 --> 21:01.813
Don't you want to become an engineer?

21:02.924 --> 21:03.985
See you then?

21:04.370 --> 21:05.897
See you, Samkutty!

21:10.487 --> 21:12.048
What happened, man?
What's the issue?

21:12.049 --> 21:13.061
Nothing.

21:13.062 --> 21:14.137
All good, man?

21:19.034 --> 21:20.654
- Let go of me!
- I'm not even holding you!

21:21.406 --> 21:23.617
Hey, kid. It’s 15 rupees per bottle.

21:29.071 --> 21:30.103
Whatever!

21:38.989 --> 21:40.095
Brother, here.

21:42.641 --> 21:43.721
How much?

21:49.367 --> 21:50.468
Bro...

21:53.857 --> 21:55.710
You... why'd you come without calling?

21:58.127 --> 21:59.507
I did call. Couldn't reach you.

22:00.046 --> 22:01.806
Yeah... I changed my number.

22:05.431 --> 22:07.484
- I'll keep my bag inside and come.
- Yeah, go ahead.

22:08.789 --> 22:10.322
When are you coming home, brother?

22:10.892 --> 22:12.379
I will... I'll come.

22:12.852 --> 22:14.132
How are classes going?

22:16.002 --> 22:18.635
It's not as easy as I thought
to get things rolling.

22:19.041 --> 22:20.215
Means?

22:21.448 --> 22:23.373
I mean... the graphics and all...

22:26.348 --> 22:28.093
So there's no fest this year either?

22:28.094 --> 22:30.261
There is. The fest will happen this time.

22:30.694 --> 22:32.878
Talks are going on with the management.

22:33.740 --> 22:37.200
The kids in the college troll groups are
really cursing me.

22:37.320 --> 22:38.487
You noticed that?

22:38.813 --> 22:41.999
That's just some dumb seniors
talking rubbish, brother.

22:43.775 --> 22:45.335
Can't really blame them though.

22:46.796 --> 22:49.843
The thousand different probabilities of
what I could've done that day,

22:50.771 --> 22:51.965
I thought about them all.

22:52.704 --> 22:54.131
But the worst happened...

22:54.996 --> 22:56.811
Maybe that's just how fate works.

22:59.533 --> 23:01.199
Do you get what I'm saying?

23:02.315 --> 23:03.528
Leave it, brother.

23:03.929 --> 23:06.045
We've spoken about this enough already.

23:06.733 --> 23:08.486
Yeah... true.

23:28.015 --> 23:29.447
Bro... where are you going?

23:29.448 --> 23:33.308
That... my bike is at the workplace.
I'll go get it.

23:34.158 --> 23:35.318
You go to bed.

23:35.557 --> 23:36.670
I'll be back.

23:36.824 --> 23:37.856
Brother...

23:39.172 --> 23:40.232
Don't go.

23:41.397 --> 23:42.775
Just because you're my brother,

23:42.776 --> 23:44.760
you're facing a lot of crap
at college, right?

23:44.761 --> 23:45.918
No, bro.

23:45.919 --> 23:47.040
Sorry.

23:48.109 --> 23:49.476
It didn't happen because of you.

23:50.115 --> 23:52.433
I did it...
so the students could enjoy the fest...

23:52.434 --> 23:53.721
Brother, sit down.

23:55.880 --> 23:57.480
I've lost everything. Even her...

24:01.379 --> 24:02.392
Brother...

24:03.665 --> 24:05.731
My life’s completely screwed right now.

24:06.823 --> 24:08.069
I'm in a trap.

24:09.350 --> 24:11.657
Life stuck me in a loop
and keeps beating me down.

24:12.632 --> 24:13.839
Don't cry, brother.

24:16.056 --> 24:18.743
I don't feel anything anymore, Samkutty.

24:25.983 --> 24:27.199
Everything will be okay.

24:52.003 --> 24:53.576
You're quite something, Samkutty.

24:55.694 --> 24:57.167
I was unable to cry.

25:00.507 --> 25:01.580
Thanks.

25:07.311 --> 25:08.324
And then?

25:12.415 --> 25:14.083
Brother... brother...

25:19.383 --> 25:21.228
So there's no fest this year either?

25:39.401 --> 25:40.587
Hey, Parashu.

25:40.701 --> 25:42.047
<i>Yeah, tell me, man.</i>

25:43.677 --> 25:45.845
We have to pull off the fest this time.
No matter what.

25:45.846 --> 25:47.392
I'm dead serious.

25:49.789 --> 25:51.146
We should bring my brother

25:51.282 --> 25:53.108
and everyone from his batch too.

26:08.617 --> 26:10.686
Look at those guys, absolutely killing it!

26:10.687 --> 26:12.671
Dude, our college
doesn’t even have a fest. Nothing!

26:12.672 --> 26:14.390
Our college sucks, man!

26:14.391 --> 26:15.423
Seriously!

26:15.424 --> 26:17.697
It wasn’t always this pathetic.

26:17.698 --> 26:20.357
CET has Dhwani, NIT has Ragam,
IIT has Saarang.

26:20.358 --> 26:22.603
Our college had a fest
that stood just as tall.

26:22.604 --> 26:23.837
Arohan Fest.

26:23.838 --> 26:25.323
Arohan was the face of this college.

26:25.324 --> 26:27.709
- Arohan fest was the emotion
of the students here. - Come, let's go.

26:27.710 --> 26:28.756
We've got classes.

26:30.069 --> 26:32.450
Don’t give up, don't give up! Keep going!

26:32.451 --> 26:34.596
But what do we even get
out of hosting this fest?

26:34.597 --> 26:36.403
There are plenty of perks!

26:36.404 --> 26:37.973
We can bunk classes with attendance.

26:37.974 --> 26:40.043
Can roam around hunting for sponsors.

26:40.044 --> 26:43.361
And students from other colleges
will visit our college too.

26:43.362 --> 26:44.454
So what?

26:45.186 --> 26:48.708
Girls from women’s colleges like LBS
and St. Teresa’s will show up!

26:49.669 --> 26:53.153
Do you know how many relationships
Arohan Fest has sparked?

26:53.277 --> 26:55.521
Look, we also want to conduct a fest here.

26:55.522 --> 26:57.068
But we need sanction for that, right?

26:57.069 --> 26:59.349
- We will get it! And if we don’t,
we’ll protest till we do! -Yeah!

26:59.350 --> 27:01.788
Excuse me.
you’re the one protesting?

27:03.176 --> 27:06.304
You are the least qualified
and the most unfit person for the job, man!

27:06.305 --> 27:07.506
Hey, "Vaan!"

27:07.507 --> 27:08.702
Who's that?!

27:09.648 --> 27:11.372
Sperm boy, you can’t pull that off!

27:11.373 --> 27:14.539
Guys, the canteen’s got
fresh cream buns today!

27:14.540 --> 27:16.014
Come on, it’s my treat.

27:16.015 --> 27:17.647
- Alright then.
- Come, come!

27:20.207 --> 27:21.902
<i>♪ Look at him! Look at him!
Look at him! ♪</i>

27:21.903 --> 27:23.738
<i>♪ He's an analytical boy! ♪</i>

27:23.739 --> 27:25.212
<i>♪ He walks in, he talks, he rocks ♪</i>

27:25.213 --> 27:26.751
<i>♪ It's a total cinematic scene! ♪</i>

27:26.752 --> 27:28.193
<i>♪ Loving, living, leading ♪</i>

27:28.194 --> 27:30.025
Will any future generation
ever witness a fest again?

27:30.026 --> 27:31.430
Hey, Samkutty…

27:31.657 --> 27:32.945
He still hasn’t dropped this?

27:32.946 --> 27:33.954
No way!

27:35.523 --> 27:37.423
Which idiot did this?!

27:38.095 --> 27:39.165
<i>♪ What a...! ♪</i>

27:39.306 --> 27:41.172
<i>♪ Loving, living, leading ♪</i>

27:41.431 --> 27:42.658
<i>♪ What a tragic...! ♪</i>

27:42.659 --> 27:44.097
<i>♪ Look at him! Look at him!
Look at him! ♪</i>

27:49.898 --> 27:51.221
Swathi R. Krishna?!

28:03.496 --> 28:06.613
<i>♪ What a tragedy,
A college with zero magic! ♪</i>

28:07.650 --> 28:09.735
Request for Arohan.

28:09.877 --> 28:11.086
Bloody nutcase!

28:14.430 --> 28:15.582
Okay, sir. I’ll come.

28:15.583 --> 28:16.817
Okay.

28:17.242 --> 28:18.412
Who was that?

28:18.601 --> 28:19.927
A call from the college.

28:20.152 --> 28:21.791
Apparently Samkutty went and submitted

28:21.792 --> 28:24.621
a request to the Bishop for Arohan Fest.
Right in the middle of the Mass!

28:24.622 --> 28:28.113
This is My body and My blood.

28:28.339 --> 28:29.378
Amen.

28:30.733 --> 28:32.167
Such a crazy boy!

28:32.278 --> 28:34.886
Not saying this because he’s your son,

28:34.996 --> 28:37.160
but Samkutty always amazes me.

28:38.245 --> 28:40.723
The hair, the style...

28:40.872 --> 28:43.575
walking around flexing
those muscles...

28:44.098 --> 28:47.488
He’s very impressed with himself, brother.

28:48.084 --> 28:49.855
The kid's a phenomenon.

28:50.210 --> 28:51.858
You should accept that at least now.

28:52.046 --> 28:53.054
Phenomenon?!

28:53.238 --> 28:55.224
All that damn “talent” crashed on my chest

28:55.225 --> 28:57.296
and there went his scholarship!

28:57.578 --> 28:59.388
Looks like the fest is his latest thrill.

28:59.506 --> 29:02.082
Just time-pass!
As if he’ll really run that fest!

29:02.772 --> 29:04.598
Still, I’m his fan.

29:04.599 --> 29:05.686
Fan of what?!

29:05.687 --> 29:08.247
You know that rusted bus
lying in the college ground, right?

29:08.487 --> 29:10.887
Looks great, kids climb
all over it for photos.

29:10.888 --> 29:12.342
But what's the point? No engine!

29:12.343 --> 29:13.545
He’s just like that.

29:14.942 --> 29:17.632
All noise, crisis management,
punch dialogues...

29:17.633 --> 29:18.741
but no engine!

29:20.271 --> 29:22.162
B... but engines are outdated now...

29:22.163 --> 29:24.083
everything’s EV these days.
Electric.

29:24.084 --> 29:25.163
Electric vehicle?

29:25.287 --> 29:27.021
Man, I’m talking about Samkutty here!

29:27.022 --> 29:28.433
He’s got no engine!

29:29.316 --> 29:31.771
I actually came to fix the fan.

29:31.772 --> 29:33.233
You doing alright, son?

29:34.695 --> 29:35.703
All the best!

29:35.967 --> 29:36.975
Thank you.

29:39.343 --> 29:40.351
Hey...

29:40.742 --> 29:42.458
- Do you think he heard that?
- Yes, he did.

29:42.459 --> 29:43.554
Damn!

29:43.710 --> 29:45.694
It’s fine. Just say sorry to him.

29:45.695 --> 29:47.450
Nothing that a sorry can’t fix.

29:47.810 --> 29:49.467
He’s your son. Just tell him.
No big deal.

30:04.640 --> 30:05.648
Tell him.

30:06.226 --> 30:07.257
Good night.

30:09.178 --> 30:10.467
G.. good night, right?

30:28.593 --> 30:30.476
Dear Wilson Uncle,

30:30.477 --> 30:31.857
- Hey...
- Bro?

30:31.999 --> 30:34.310
Today’s company is the only one
hiring students with arrears.

30:34.311 --> 30:35.396
You’re not coming?

30:35.397 --> 30:37.402
It's probably
some organ-trafficking company.

30:37.804 --> 30:39.333
What are you writing?

30:39.498 --> 30:41.999
It’s an item for Arohan.

30:42.351 --> 30:44.077
Dude, aren’t you done yet?

30:44.078 --> 30:45.810
Our college life is almost over.

30:46.191 --> 30:49.037
From the Ombudsman to Child Welfare,
you’ve sent letters to everyone!

30:49.327 --> 30:51.202
Even Swathi, whom you kept chasing,

30:51.203 --> 30:53.429
has already gone through
her second breakup.

30:55.249 --> 30:57.083
The world’s moved on.

30:57.084 --> 30:59.777
And you’re still here
with letters and your concrete fetish!

31:01.073 --> 31:02.968
What’s this?
You even printed WhatsApp chats?!

31:04.296 --> 31:06.465
“Hi, chetta... no reply."

31:07.568 --> 31:08.998
Vineeth Sreenivasan?!

31:10.412 --> 31:11.826
Of course!

31:12.325 --> 31:14.380
Hey! Grand!

31:14.381 --> 31:15.764
Just wait and watch, my boy!

31:16.537 --> 31:19.598
All my earlier plans
had just one thing missing.

31:19.811 --> 31:20.819
What?

31:21.149 --> 31:22.157
Emotion.

31:23.133 --> 31:25.470
But this time,
we’ll definitely get the sanction.

31:25.630 --> 31:26.679
Because...

31:26.680 --> 31:27.711
Because?

31:27.712 --> 31:30.469
You’re the key part of my plan, bro.

31:30.566 --> 31:31.838
Really?

31:32.110 --> 31:33.461
Then I’ll sign twice!

31:33.462 --> 31:34.470
Go on, sign.

31:38.579 --> 31:40.837
Then we’ll head straight to the office.

31:41.907 --> 31:44.250
Those are the parents
of the students who died that day.

31:45.647 --> 31:48.241
The one getting out of that car
is Merin chechi’s father.

31:48.468 --> 31:50.095
So… shall we go in?

31:50.276 --> 31:52.064
Why are they all here?

31:53.352 --> 31:55.476
Madam, it’s been almost five years now.

31:56.305 --> 31:58.196
That fest belongs to the students here.

31:58.197 --> 32:00.205
We all wish to see it restarted.

32:00.206 --> 32:01.251
I have a request...

32:01.252 --> 32:04.182
Please open the auditorium
and let events happen again, madam.

32:04.276 --> 32:05.462
Well... I...

32:05.463 --> 32:06.886
What I mean is...

32:06.887 --> 32:09.306
The students here
really want the fest back.

32:09.547 --> 32:12.399
Until that happens,
our children keep getting blamed for it.

32:12.400 --> 32:13.594
Exactly.

32:13.595 --> 32:16.368
That’s... quite difficult for us.

32:17.148 --> 32:19.265
Madam, just see this.

32:19.393 --> 32:22.291
These are petitions students
have sent to our homes.

32:22.437 --> 32:24.343
We receive 10-15 of these every day.

32:24.344 --> 32:25.584
And phone calls too.

32:25.875 --> 32:28.032
There should be some limit, right?

32:28.305 --> 32:30.735
Well...
maybe a few students are interested.

32:31.344 --> 32:32.578
Sir, today is my birthday.

32:32.706 --> 32:35.086
- How old are you today?
<i>- There aren’t really any events in college.</i>

32:35.087 --> 32:37.050
Shouldn’t we conduct Arohan fest?

32:37.051 --> 32:38.768
Most students are still focused on studies.

32:38.769 --> 32:39.861
<i>Arohan Fest...?</i>

32:39.862 --> 32:41.454
- Huh?! Digambaran?! From which batch?!
- <i>Your age!</i>

32:41.455 --> 32:43.603
- <i>I asked your age!</i>
- About the Arohan... Arohan Fest?

32:43.604 --> 32:44.899
Who's Paloli Mohammed Kutty?

32:44.900 --> 32:46.658
- What’s going on there? You, come here.
- Madam, this guy!

32:46.659 --> 32:47.578
Hold this!

32:47.579 --> 32:49.147
- Yes, madam.
- What’s the issue?

32:49.969 --> 32:52.123
My friend Parashu... I mean, Prashanth...

32:52.124 --> 32:54.187
says he’s quitting this college.

32:54.188 --> 32:55.468
Huh? When?!

32:55.587 --> 32:56.595
What's the reason?

32:57.368 --> 33:00.159
He says there’s no fest
or entertainment in this college.

33:00.384 --> 33:03.121
You mean, that Prashanth Raj from S7
with 32 arrears?

33:03.122 --> 33:05.237
<i>He should definitely quit this college.</i>

33:05.238 --> 33:07.026
Let him go! Let him go!
Tell him to leave.

33:07.714 --> 33:08.972
So, the problem’s solved then?

33:08.973 --> 33:11.800
<i>If that’s what Prashanth wants,
let him do it.</i>

33:11.962 --> 33:13.245
Nothing else, right?

33:13.815 --> 33:15.236
Let it be, madam.

33:15.237 --> 33:17.465
But what made him think like that?

33:17.466 --> 33:19.349
Isn’t that what we should be looking at?

33:20.018 --> 33:22.899
Madam, before we graduate,
we just want to witness Arohan Fest once.

33:24.174 --> 33:26.758
Plus, during the last NAAC accreditation,

33:26.759 --> 33:28.283
we missed the A certificate.

33:28.284 --> 33:31.376
Because we didn’t have extra-curricular
like Onam celebrations or a fest.

33:31.377 --> 33:33.282
Axing a flagship fest halfway

33:33.283 --> 33:35.540
will definitely leave a black mark
on your career, madam.

33:35.752 --> 33:38.024
If you say 'no' today, nothing changes.

33:38.025 --> 33:40.390
Tomorrow will just be another boring day...
No... Forget it!

33:40.391 --> 33:42.741
We must conduct this fest,
no matter what, madam.

33:43.151 --> 33:45.290
Poor my friend Parashu wakes up from sleep

33:45.376 --> 33:47.469
shouting “Arohan Fest! Arohan Fest!”

33:47.470 --> 33:48.641
Don’t overdo it, man!

33:48.642 --> 33:52.367
This fest should be dedicated
to Chitra chechi who left us--

33:52.368 --> 33:53.550
Chaithra.

33:53.551 --> 33:54.682
Ch... Chaitra chechi,

33:54.683 --> 33:57.749
Merin chechi, Akhil chettan...
to all of them, madam.

34:00.635 --> 34:01.978
If this fest happens,

34:01.979 --> 34:04.618
they’ll be happy watching from heaven.

34:08.851 --> 34:10.101
It worked!

34:11.875 --> 34:12.882
Oh, sorry.

34:13.070 --> 34:14.350
I got a bit emotional.

34:14.351 --> 34:15.842
You were having
a staff meeting here, right?

34:15.843 --> 34:17.045
- That's okay.
- I’m sorry, guys.

34:17.046 --> 34:18.373
Praise the Lord. Amen.

34:18.585 --> 34:20.108
All the best.

34:24.931 --> 34:26.321
Uncle...

34:27.247 --> 34:30.064
I just... saw you upstairs...

34:30.065 --> 34:31.424
Ah!

34:33.163 --> 34:35.555
Well... the students also plan to release

34:35.556 --> 34:38.639
Merin chechi’s magazine during the fest,

34:38.640 --> 34:41.249
the one that couldn’t be released that day.

34:43.139 --> 34:44.576
That’s good.

34:47.022 --> 34:48.030
And, uncle...

34:50.484 --> 34:51.492
Sorry.

34:52.054 --> 34:53.062
For what?

34:54.140 --> 34:55.460
Nothing... just like that.

34:56.148 --> 34:58.187
In the principal’s room… I was just...

35:08.712 --> 35:10.718
<i>Good morning, sir. This is FRI,</i>

35:10.719 --> 35:12.248
<i>Frequency Resonance Injector.</i>

35:12.249 --> 35:15.023
<i>With this,
we can trip the brain of any system.</i>

35:15.024 --> 35:17.890
But this system was invented
to help people, right?

35:18.165 --> 35:20.655
Then why are you trying
to trip it for no reason?

35:24.204 --> 35:25.212
Sir, shall we start?

35:26.509 --> 35:27.874
Sir, safety glass.

35:29.603 --> 35:30.610
- Light.
- Oh!

35:36.001 --> 35:38.601
Sir, could you stand a little aside?
It’s about to shoot at high speed.

35:38.602 --> 35:40.945
If it hits you,
you’ll turn into a slab on the spot.

35:40.946 --> 35:42.024
Really?

35:42.025 --> 35:43.351
Who the hell is this guy?

35:43.352 --> 35:45.195
Those at the back, move aside, move!

35:45.196 --> 35:46.366
Hey, move back!

35:46.367 --> 35:48.038
Your skull will crack open! Move!

35:49.305 --> 35:50.968
Sir, just a little to the side.

35:54.032 --> 35:55.696
<i>♪ Take a note now
He is a wanna be! ♪</i>

35:55.697 --> 35:57.618
<i>♪ He is kind a cooler
Let him, let him be ♪</i>

35:57.899 --> 35:59.742
<i>♪ Dreamer Dreamer Dreamer
Little skibidi ♪</i>

35:59.860 --> 36:01.978
<i>♪ Oh no Mama !
What a What a tragedy ♪</i>

36:03.032 --> 36:04.040
Awesome!

36:11.594 --> 36:12.626
Hey!

36:12.627 --> 36:15.048
Is this for grinding
betel leaves and areca nut?

36:15.251 --> 36:17.258
Is this your "instant concreting?"

36:17.742 --> 36:20.474
Is this the crap you're going
to save the Mullaperiyar dam with?

36:22.325 --> 36:25.177
Sir, just like instant coffee,
this is instant concrete.

36:25.178 --> 36:26.294
This is just the beta version.

36:26.295 --> 36:28.662
Once the full version comes,
we can even seal blocks underwater!

36:28.663 --> 36:30.021
I’ll seal a block on your head!

36:30.155 --> 36:32.626
Why are you so obsessed
with concrete anyway?

36:33.485 --> 36:35.280
Just get lost, man! Here!

36:36.478 --> 36:37.485
Take this too.

36:37.828 --> 36:39.027
Move it like this.

36:39.028 --> 36:40.128
On this side...

36:40.462 --> 36:42.422
Samkutty, do you know
where all I searched for you?

36:42.423 --> 36:44.024
Wait till you hear what I found out!

36:44.025 --> 36:46.859
<i>Dear students,
there’s an important announcement.</i>

36:47.141 --> 36:49.460
<i>Before that, let me remind you,</i>

36:50.093 --> 36:53.585
<i>BCET College still prioritizes academics.</i>

36:54.256 --> 36:57.647
<i>After many discussions and review meetings,</i>

36:58.623 --> 37:01.729
<i>so, it is my immense pleasure to announce,</i>

37:03.189 --> 37:05.442
<i>the management has finally approved</i>

37:05.663 --> 37:08.113
- <i>Arohan Fest!</i>
- YAY!

37:09.028 --> 37:10.277
Superb!

37:10.278 --> 37:11.739
Nailed it!

37:11.740 --> 37:13.115
You did it, man!

37:16.496 --> 37:18.304
I came looking for you
just to tell you this.

37:18.305 --> 37:20.124
You should be the convener of Arohan Fest!

37:20.125 --> 37:22.077
Here, your concrete tilak!

37:22.078 --> 37:23.281
YAY!!!

37:26.039 --> 37:28.488
Arohan! Arohan! Arohan!

37:28.624 --> 37:31.248
Arohan! Arohan! Arohan!

37:31.249 --> 37:32.671
Arohan!

37:35.146 --> 37:36.304
Arohan! Arohan! Arohan!

37:36.305 --> 37:37.865
So, after all these years of waiting,

37:37.866 --> 37:40.002
our Aarohan Fest has finally been approved.

37:40.003 --> 37:42.249
And this is going to be its first meeting.

37:42.345 --> 37:46.124
This time the management
is planning Arohan on a grand scale.

37:46.125 --> 37:47.601
I’m pretty excited about it.

37:47.602 --> 37:50.238
Speaking about Arohan Fest...

37:50.540 --> 37:51.790
What's wrong?

37:52.056 --> 37:54.587
- The gateways of Ananthapuri--
- Sorry, we have got class.

37:54.975 --> 37:56.434
To hell with the fest. I’m going home.

37:56.435 --> 37:57.540
Sir, this for BTS.

37:57.541 --> 37:58.572
What? DTS?!

37:58.573 --> 37:59.999
Not DTS, it's BTS, sir.

38:00.000 --> 38:01.557
- Did you get your record signed?
- No.

38:02.775 --> 38:04.317
- Yes.
- Brother...

38:05.008 --> 38:06.444
The fest got approved.

38:06.775 --> 38:07.782
Ah!

38:08.633 --> 38:09.836
Good for you all, man.

38:10.922 --> 38:11.930
Make it grand.

38:12.204 --> 38:13.212
YES!

38:13.832 --> 38:14.972
Okay.

38:15.333 --> 38:16.604
YES!

38:19.154 --> 38:21.938
So now that the fest is on,

38:21.939 --> 38:23.626
who’s our convener?

38:24.317 --> 38:25.886
Who else?

38:25.988 --> 38:28.032
Our very own Samkutty!

38:30.849 --> 38:32.852
Climb up, bro!
Climb on my back!

38:36.795 --> 38:43.286
Convener! Convener! Convener!

38:43.287 --> 38:44.903
Conve...

38:45.061 --> 38:46.158
What's this?

38:46.159 --> 38:49.237
Finally,
my relentless efforts have paid off.

38:49.370 --> 38:52.339
So many meetings, memorandums, letters!

38:52.340 --> 38:54.564
And at last,
our fest is officially sanctioned.

38:54.935 --> 38:55.943
Thank God.

38:56.283 --> 38:58.004
Our students are so thrilled.

38:58.307 --> 38:59.409
Personally, me too.

38:59.410 --> 39:02.252
Our union sees this as a huge opportunity.

39:02.253 --> 39:03.475
Especially me!

39:03.804 --> 39:04.961
I'm grateful.

39:04.962 --> 39:06.091
Very good, Vivi.

39:06.282 --> 39:10.405
Only collect funds from
students who are willing to contribute.

39:10.577 --> 39:11.602
Whew! I’m spared!

39:11.603 --> 39:14.321
- Let Swathi be the main convener.
- Wow, congrats!

39:14.322 --> 39:17.257
Vivi and the UUC representatives
will assist her.

39:17.844 --> 39:18.852
Okay?

39:19.196 --> 39:20.204
Okay, sir?

39:20.695 --> 39:22.998
Now... is there anyone else?

39:26.602 --> 39:28.051
What the hell?!

39:28.052 --> 39:29.904
Why is that freeloader
stealing your credit?

39:29.905 --> 39:30.937
That guy, Vivi!

39:30.938 --> 39:32.740
<i>Alright, the general body meeting
is concluded.</i>

39:32.741 --> 39:33.749
Next...

39:33.945 --> 39:35.832
Hey, are you crying?

39:36.431 --> 39:38.210
Get down.

39:38.860 --> 39:40.285
- Oh, no.
- Sam...

39:41.241 --> 39:43.191
I knew this would happen.

39:46.559 --> 39:48.024
Let whoever wants be the convener.

39:48.025 --> 39:49.033
Bro...

39:49.235 --> 39:52.356
Just remind them about that magazine.

39:55.072 --> 39:56.244
Concrete crap.

39:56.396 --> 39:57.551
I'm leaving.

39:57.552 --> 39:59.477
Hey, no. Stop there.
Come with me.

39:59.478 --> 40:01.896
You can't just walk away!
Let's demand answers!

40:01.897 --> 40:03.741
- Hey, congratulations!
- Where are you all going? Sit down!

40:03.742 --> 40:05.295
Where are you going?
Meeting's not over. Sit down there!

40:05.296 --> 40:06.685
Wow, Samkutty chettan!

40:06.851 --> 40:09.869
Madam, Samkutty is the one
who bled for this fest,

40:09.870 --> 40:11.528
sacrificing his own studies!

40:11.529 --> 40:13.178
At least include him in some committee.

40:13.179 --> 40:14.300
Oh please!

40:15.806 --> 40:16.973
Look at this.

40:17.107 --> 40:20.521
Proof that he already contacted
Vineeth Sreenivasan for the ProShow.

40:20.696 --> 40:22.220
- Guys!
- Vineeth Sreenivasan?!

40:22.524 --> 40:23.595
Who's that?

40:24.779 --> 40:25.981
Whoa!

40:26.130 --> 40:27.532
That's not possible, madam.

40:27.533 --> 40:29.019
He has around 25 arrears.

40:29.020 --> 40:30.152
Shut up, man!

40:30.153 --> 40:32.340
You even have a supply
in Environmental Science, right?

40:32.434 --> 40:33.507
Shameful.

40:33.508 --> 40:35.848
If he can't even write two lines
about global warming,

40:35.849 --> 40:37.872
how will he handle a fest?

40:37.873 --> 40:39.044
Hey, you!

40:39.045 --> 40:40.894
We know climate change is real.

40:40.895 --> 40:43.997
What did you do for the fest, other than
stuffing your face with cream buns?

40:43.998 --> 40:45.122
Answer me, mister.

40:45.835 --> 40:47.038
Madam...

40:55.510 --> 40:56.787
Are you crying?

40:58.102 --> 40:59.149
Caught him!

41:00.081 --> 41:01.089
No.

41:01.260 --> 41:03.857
Are you upset
that you didn't make it to the committee?

41:04.448 --> 41:05.456
No.

41:07.487 --> 41:08.756
I have a cold.

41:09.854 --> 41:11.349
Here, cough once.

41:13.437 --> 41:15.616
What is this,
a general ward at a medical college?

41:15.955 --> 41:17.085
Madam, he’s been camping

41:17.086 --> 41:19.896
outside the office
with this excuse for years.

41:19.897 --> 41:22.241
If this guy jumps off
the college roof,

41:22.242 --> 41:23.514
we'll be in trouble!

41:23.515 --> 41:25.271
Yes! Yes! He might jump, madam!

41:26.040 --> 41:28.079
Just squeeze him into some committee, madam!

41:28.080 --> 41:29.321
Please...

41:29.878 --> 41:32.150
Madam, honestly, the one most qualified

41:32.151 --> 41:34.299
to convene Arohan Fest is Samkutty.

41:34.300 --> 41:37.173
No one has obsessed over this fest
like he has.

41:37.665 --> 41:38.705
I know that.

41:38.706 --> 41:40.119
And you know, because of this

41:40.120 --> 41:42.034
we even nicknamed him "Fest Man."

41:42.035 --> 41:43.556
- Right? We call him that.
- Yes.

41:44.953 --> 41:47.730
Even his seminar topic was about the fest.

41:47.731 --> 41:49.187
He literally argued in the seminar

41:49.188 --> 41:52.249
that lack of fests causes mental breakdowns
in students!

41:53.961 --> 41:55.260
And about his arrears,

41:55.261 --> 41:57.791
I believe he has cleared most of them.

41:58.575 --> 41:59.716
Right?

42:01.721 --> 42:04.535
So it’s only fair
that Samkutty heads the fest.

42:07.143 --> 42:09.694
When we’ve got someone this passionate,

42:09.695 --> 42:11.795
why look for anyone else?

42:12.085 --> 42:14.983
So please include Samkutty
in the committee, madam.

42:21.352 --> 42:23.610
Alright then,
the Arohan committee is formed.

42:23.937 --> 42:26.244
Event head - Swathi.
Media Head - Elizabath.

42:26.245 --> 42:28.074
Discipline Committee head - Jibin.

42:28.405 --> 42:30.110
As usual, the discipline committee
is full of troublemakers.

42:30.111 --> 42:31.861
And the one who cried and begged…
Sorry…

42:31.862 --> 42:33.742
the one who sneaked in
through the emotional wild card,

42:33.743 --> 42:34.858
Samkutty, is our convener.

42:34.859 --> 42:36.457
I didn’t cry. I just had a cold!

42:36.458 --> 42:37.861
- Cold!
- Okay, blow your nose.

42:38.084 --> 42:40.037
We should arrange a photo
with Vineeth Sreenivasan too.

42:40.038 --> 42:41.360
Samkutty chetta! I’m Bosco,

42:41.361 --> 42:42.850
1500 meters, state level,

42:42.851 --> 42:44.240
in first year now.

42:44.392 --> 42:46.708
If you need anything, just tell me.

42:47.306 --> 42:49.178
Actually, I’m a hidden gem.

42:49.179 --> 42:50.722
Ah, impressive.

42:51.943 --> 42:54.427
Man, she's there. Just go and talk.

42:54.811 --> 42:57.314
Anagha... Anagha...
The principal is calling you.

42:57.315 --> 42:59.314
Go there. There.. there...
Just come here.

42:59.315 --> 43:00.338
Something’s going on there.

43:00.339 --> 43:01.970
Swathi, thank you so much.

43:02.147 --> 43:03.825
Actually I’m happy for you, Samkutty.

43:03.826 --> 43:06.325
Everyone here knows
how hard you worked for this fest.

43:06.859 --> 43:07.955
You really deserve it.

43:10.863 --> 43:12.919
We’re good between us, right?

43:13.560 --> 43:14.837
I’m okay.

43:15.009 --> 43:17.500
You were the one who proposed
and then ran off that day.

43:17.501 --> 43:19.257
After that you barely even looked at me.

43:19.629 --> 43:20.924
Well...

43:21.205 --> 43:23.049
I got a bit busy after that.

43:23.050 --> 43:24.234
Oh, busy?

43:24.235 --> 43:26.133
Anyway, I was just
too young and immature then.

43:26.134 --> 43:27.734
Nothing like that now.

43:27.891 --> 43:29.111
Too young?!

43:29.650 --> 43:31.921
Anyway, my friends say

43:31.922 --> 43:34.968
your proposal that day
should be turned into a research paper.

43:38.058 --> 43:43.115
Meanwhile, you were in a relationship
with some Navy guy, right?

43:43.459 --> 43:44.811
That... didn’t really work out.

43:44.812 --> 43:45.999
- Oh wow.
- <i>Swathi... Swathi...</i>

43:46.000 --> 43:48.119
- I mean... I’m sorry.
- Swathi, come to office. -One second.

43:49.369 --> 43:51.728
- Sam, we’re going to run the fest now.
- Yes.

43:51.729 --> 43:53.937
It’s serious business. A big task.

43:53.938 --> 43:55.468
So no more childish stuff, okay?

43:55.469 --> 43:57.577
Yes! Of course, Swathi.
It's a simple crisis.

43:58.741 --> 43:59.944
And Swathi...

44:01.153 --> 44:02.670
I really did have a cold.

44:02.874 --> 44:06.061
Basically I’m not someone
who cries in any situation.

44:06.544 --> 44:07.921
What’s wrong with that?

44:07.922 --> 44:10.366
Guys who cry when they’re emotional
are hot. Okay?

44:14.937 --> 44:16.389
What did she say at the end?

44:18.458 --> 44:19.787
That I’m hot!

44:19.788 --> 44:20.788
Hot?!

44:20.906 --> 44:22.083
Man, you’re there!

44:22.217 --> 44:23.249
Really?

44:23.250 --> 44:24.274
You’re on another level now!

44:24.275 --> 44:26.159
Fest sorted and romance sorted
on the same day!

44:28.265 --> 44:30.069
Now no one can stop me.

45:04.266 --> 45:08.134
<i>♪ O, Mother, my warm blanket ♪</i>

45:08.670 --> 45:11.205
<i>Tomorrow evening at BCET College,</i>

45:11.302 --> 45:13.208
<i>as part of Arohan Fest,</i>

45:13.209 --> 45:16.432
<i>the sensational pride of Malayalam cinema,</i>

45:16.623 --> 45:20.585
<i>actor, director, singer,
writer and producer...</i>

45:20.586 --> 45:22.538
<i>Vineeth Sreenivasan,</i>

45:22.657 --> 45:24.303
<i>live in ProShow!</i>

45:24.507 --> 45:25.937
Hey, Vadi!

45:26.440 --> 45:27.503
Yes, bro!

45:27.504 --> 45:28.890
The tip of this mic is rusted.

45:28.891 --> 45:30.929
Call those guys and
ask them to bring a proper one.

45:30.930 --> 45:31.967
Okay, I’ll call them now.

45:31.968 --> 45:33.856
The sound’s all scattered.
Can’t hear a thing.

45:34.116 --> 45:36.061
Stop chatting and go get the thing.

45:36.328 --> 45:37.895
Bring it right now. Got it?

45:37.896 --> 45:40.335
- I told you not to include these fellows.
- What can I do!

45:40.513 --> 45:41.614
Bro,

45:41.615 --> 45:44.115
the new mic’s coming from Muruga now.
I’ve already called him.

45:44.604 --> 45:47.471
This Vineeth Sreenivasan ProShow,
will that be a challenge for us?

45:47.472 --> 45:48.667
What show is that, Vadi?

45:48.668 --> 45:50.558
It’s a big musical show.

45:51.615 --> 45:54.616
Hey, how much would
Vineeth Sreenivasan’s program cost?

45:54.714 --> 45:55.901
A rough figure?

45:56.458 --> 45:57.490
At least ten...

45:57.491 --> 45:58.498
Ten lakh.

45:58.982 --> 46:00.658
Ten lakh?!

46:01.196 --> 46:03.210
Does money mean nothing anymore?

46:03.519 --> 46:05.691
They’re college kids, bro.
It’s a big event.

46:05.692 --> 46:06.916
And in the evening

46:06.917 --> 46:08.963
they’re planning a bike rally
from our Nemom ground too.

46:08.964 --> 46:10.322
Bro.

46:10.756 --> 46:12.466
This is Varkala Sudheesh.

46:12.928 --> 46:14.186
Our own guy.

46:14.187 --> 46:15.782
Sounds exactly like Vineeth Sreenivasan.

46:15.894 --> 46:17.192
Sings brilliantly.

46:17.193 --> 46:19.150
Even looks almost like him.

46:19.437 --> 46:20.469
Shall we bring him?

46:20.470 --> 46:22.463
We can get him
for about eight thousand rupees.

46:22.464 --> 46:23.634
Just place him after your program.

46:23.635 --> 46:24.979
No need for all that.

46:24.980 --> 46:26.339
You just hold the mic
and hum a little, bro.

46:26.340 --> 46:27.799
The crowd will go wild, right?

46:27.800 --> 46:28.910
Of course.

46:29.186 --> 46:30.194
Kuttan bro,

46:30.757 --> 46:32.467
your photo looks a bit small.

46:32.468 --> 46:34.486
That brat's coat fills half the poster.

46:35.012 --> 46:36.259
Where is he?

46:36.260 --> 46:37.399
There he is.

46:41.118 --> 46:42.517
Let go of it, man.

46:42.764 --> 46:45.062
After all, Agnivesh has won prizes
in Super Singer.

46:45.063 --> 46:46.657
What were we doing at his age?

46:46.816 --> 46:48.301
Just plucking tamarinds and mangoes!

46:48.302 --> 46:49.571
Bro, everything’s fine,

46:49.572 --> 46:51.377
but I really can’t stand
that boy’s show-off.

46:51.378 --> 46:52.877
His mouth is bigger than he is.

46:52.878 --> 46:54.811
From the moment he came,
he’s been bossing me around.

46:54.812 --> 46:56.821
Honey-coated jaggery,
ginger water, cinnamon...

46:56.822 --> 46:58.236
What is he, an elephant?

46:58.237 --> 47:00.696
A while ago he told me
to burst the firecrackers at low volume.

47:00.697 --> 47:02.625
How do you burst crackers
at low volume?

47:03.056 --> 47:04.844
Let go of it. He’s just a kid.

47:04.845 --> 47:07.407
What I’m saying is,
once the show’s over,

47:07.408 --> 47:09.016
we’ll keep you, and tear him apart.

47:10.260 --> 47:11.344
This is Agnivesh’s father.

47:11.345 --> 47:12.353
Greetings.

47:12.463 --> 47:14.191
Your son sings wonderfully.

47:14.192 --> 47:16.003
Sreekuttan chetta,
can I tell you something?

47:16.293 --> 47:18.985
It's for the first time Agnivesh
is performing on stage

47:18.986 --> 47:20.309
with a guy like you.

47:20.689 --> 47:22.075
Hello, what do you mean?!

47:22.076 --> 47:24.168
No, I’m not saying it in a bad way.

47:24.574 --> 47:27.083
Agnivesh has studied
music professionally, you see.

47:27.573 --> 47:29.932
And this song “Mother, my warm blanket”
he’s singing...

47:29.933 --> 47:30.941
Yeah...

47:31.121 --> 47:32.353
Don't worry, he’ll manage it.

47:32.354 --> 47:34.203
His voice does crack a bit
when it goes high.

47:34.814 --> 47:37.523
That’s just because his voice
is still changing. Totally normal.

47:37.801 --> 47:39.973
No, after hearing this song, he said

47:40.494 --> 47:42.621
it feels a bit amateurish.

47:42.809 --> 47:46.213
Also it seems like it was composed by
someone who doesn’t really know music.

47:46.346 --> 47:48.448
Who said Kuttan doesn't know music?

47:49.323 --> 47:51.354
Huh? He composed that song?

47:53.347 --> 47:57.384
♪ The sky bloomed in full ♪

47:58.028 --> 48:03.199
♪ In your little nest of blooms
My heart gently swell, birdie ♪

48:03.371 --> 48:04.996
♪ The river sparkles, the fields shine ♪

48:04.997 --> 48:06.031
Vadi...

48:06.581 --> 48:08.636
Okay sir, got it.
You sing well, I see that.

48:09.480 --> 48:10.847
It's not me who got a problem.

48:10.848 --> 48:12.101
You know why?

48:12.198 --> 48:14.690
Agnivesh is a bit of a hothead.

48:15.430 --> 48:16.438
He’s gotta be fiery.

48:16.564 --> 48:18.364
Only then can he cook it right!

48:18.548 --> 48:20.743
Don't worry. The show will rock.

48:21.056 --> 48:22.403
It's my word.

48:23.056 --> 48:25.461
- Come on bro, let’s have idlis.
- Got sambar?

48:25.462 --> 48:27.697
- Yeah, Sambar too.
- Alright, then I'll have them.

48:30.181 --> 48:32.154
- What’s this?
- How’s it?

48:32.879 --> 48:33.981
What?

48:33.982 --> 48:34.996
My feet.

48:34.997 --> 48:37.010
I went to the beauty parlor for a pedicure.

48:37.011 --> 48:37.994
Wow.

48:38.581 --> 48:40.324
Just help me put this on.

48:41.376 --> 48:42.384
Come on!

48:45.129 --> 48:47.024
Isn’t this a bit over the top, girl?

48:47.254 --> 48:49.386
The entire Ayyampattu family
is showing up.

48:49.511 --> 48:51.823
They've booked rooms
at Govinda Tourist Home.

48:51.824 --> 48:54.817
Auntie, grandma,
the whole clan is coming.

48:55.543 --> 48:57.855
They cursed me, said I’ll be doomed!

48:58.277 --> 48:59.878
What difference does it make if they come?

48:59.879 --> 49:02.441
They need to witness
a massive crowd cheering for you!

49:03.012 --> 49:04.911
We don’t have any riches to flaunt.

49:04.912 --> 49:06.497
So we might as well flaunt your vocals!

49:06.498 --> 49:07.849
That’s right.

49:07.850 --> 49:09.602
But ever since I tied the sacred thread,

49:09.603 --> 49:11.392
the boys say I've turned into a weakling.

49:11.753 --> 49:13.470
I'm the one who decides that!

49:14.244 --> 49:16.845
My husband is still an absolute boss!
What do those idiots know?

49:18.401 --> 49:21.960
And when you sing "Mother, my warm blanket,"
I’ll be right in the front row.

49:22.778 --> 49:24.657
Even though it’s a song about your mother,

49:24.658 --> 49:27.110
when I hear it,
I feel like you're singing it to me.

49:28.581 --> 49:29.866
Will see to it.

49:30.364 --> 49:31.937
But this is my debut.

49:32.254 --> 49:33.814
I feel a little nervous.

49:34.011 --> 49:36.725
I never got this tense,
not even for that Thuckalay issue!

49:37.799 --> 49:40.463
Don’t stress,
the Goddess is watching over you.

49:40.464 --> 49:42.608
Plus, your mother and I too.

49:43.065 --> 49:45.296
Aren’t three powerful women
enough backup for you?

49:48.182 --> 49:50.412
Dad, O! A song that starts with O!

49:50.571 --> 49:51.949
Okay, 'O', right?

49:52.057 --> 49:53.487
Yeah, let’s go…

49:53.488 --> 49:55.870
- Yeah, 'O My Precious One'
- Sing it, Dad.

49:56.239 --> 49:57.246
Sure.

49:59.463 --> 50:03.117
♪ O my precious one, come to me ♪

50:03.118 --> 50:07.423
<i>... the Arohan Fest rally
will be flagged off</i>

50:07.570 --> 50:12.507
<i>with an epic surprise flash mob
at 3:30 PM!</i>

50:12.598 --> 50:14.038
The time has finally arrived!

50:14.039 --> 50:15.411
So, BCET-ians,

50:15.412 --> 50:18.602
It's time for AROHAN!

50:19.898 --> 50:20.866
<i>♪ Acrobatic ♪</i>

50:20.867 --> 50:21.860
Wow!

50:22.612 --> 50:23.805
<i>♪ Acrobatic ♪</i>

50:23.806 --> 50:25.092
<i>♪ Problematic ♪</i>

50:25.253 --> 50:26.433
<i>♪ Acrobatic ♪</i>

50:26.553 --> 50:27.753
<i>♪ Problematic ♪</i>

50:27.900 --> 50:29.066
<i>♪ Acrobatic ♪</i>

50:29.494 --> 50:32.165
<i>♪ Right now
Aint nobody here, when we plan this ♪</i>

50:32.166 --> 50:34.830
<i>♪ By now
Everyone is owning this like true boss ♪</i>

50:34.831 --> 50:37.479
<i>♪ Lay low
Till you write a name on your pay check ♪</i>

50:37.480 --> 50:40.103
<i>♪ Say Now
Will you clean it out when the lights out ♪</i>

50:40.104 --> 50:42.824
<i>♪ Who reached for
True wisdom, the dark, and glory? ♪</i>

50:42.825 --> 50:45.265
<i>♪ Born time and again...
Who are these messengers of God? ♪</i>

50:45.266 --> 50:48.026
<i>♪ The cherished yet enslaved ones...
Who are these tormented souls? ♪</i>

50:48.027 --> 50:50.678
<i>♪ Who claims the mountain peak?
Who celebrates the triumph? ♪</i>

50:51.965 --> 50:53.299
<i>♪ Who celebrates the triumph? ♪</i>

50:54.186 --> 50:55.723
This is Atom. Arohan's mascot.

50:55.724 --> 50:57.097
It has 4 movements.

50:57.098 --> 50:58.653
Let me show you one of them now.
Uppercut.

50:58.804 --> 50:59.957
This is Arohan!

51:01.301 --> 51:03.235
Here's the list.

51:03.809 --> 51:05.018
Every thirty minutes,

51:05.019 --> 51:08.216
a secret admirer
who wishes to remain anonymous

51:08.217 --> 51:10.281
must dedicate a song to Samkutty bro.

51:10.755 --> 51:12.122
See you then?

51:12.988 --> 51:14.379
Who is this Samkutty?

51:14.466 --> 51:15.692
<i>♪ Mic check! ♪</i>

51:16.164 --> 51:17.362
Samkutty bro is iconic.

51:17.363 --> 51:19.091
A guy with a deep fascination for concrete.

51:20.199 --> 51:23.723
I wish he coordinates
the Attukal Pongala next.

51:23.724 --> 51:25.405
- Ugly boy!
- A visionary!

51:25.406 --> 51:27.498
Who the hell is he
to revive the stalled fest?

51:27.499 --> 51:28.671
Samkutty bro! Samkutty bro!

51:28.672 --> 51:30.699
This is how
Vineethettan will come up to sing.

51:31.761 --> 51:32.934
Who the hell is he?

51:32.935 --> 51:34.214
Samkutty bro! Samkutty bro!

51:34.215 --> 51:35.825
Woohoo!

51:35.826 --> 51:37.053
Nailed it, bro!

51:43.307 --> 51:44.554
- What the hell is this?
- Flash mob...

51:44.555 --> 51:46.076
Bro, it's their flash mob.

51:46.256 --> 51:48.686
They act like they're gonna fight,
then suddenly dance.

51:48.687 --> 51:50.747
It's the 'Koottukaar'
gang's idea.

51:51.922 --> 51:53.075
Yikes!

51:53.523 --> 51:55.441
What a powerful name for a gang, right?

51:55.442 --> 51:56.590
'Koottukaar'!

52:06.937 --> 52:08.437
- Hey, Bosco!
- Yeah?

52:08.846 --> 52:10.436
Keep an eye on me at all times.

52:10.437 --> 52:13.279
If any of them tries to mess with me,
finish them.

52:13.552 --> 52:15.212
Got it? You have full power of attorney.

52:15.300 --> 52:16.828
Okay bro, consider it done.

52:16.829 --> 52:18.002
That's my boy!

52:19.098 --> 52:22.302
Guys, fire and safety, ambulance,
all that needs to be managed.

52:22.303 --> 52:24.721
And isn't Parashu handling
the police clearance for the mud race?

52:24.722 --> 52:26.060
Samkutty!

52:26.061 --> 52:27.146
Swathi R Krishna?

52:27.242 --> 52:28.341
Sis...

52:28.808 --> 52:30.940
We've got some crisis management there.
Come on.

52:30.941 --> 52:32.669
Let’s just go there and do whatever.

52:33.966 --> 52:36.406
What did you respond to
Vineeth Sreenivasan's mail?

52:37.390 --> 52:39.856
He says he won't get on stage
without the payment.

52:39.959 --> 52:40.887
Swathi--

52:40.888 --> 52:44.109
You made my dad pitch in half the cash
because we don't have funds!

52:44.650 --> 52:47.763
Have you ever seen
a marble company sponsor a college fest?

52:47.764 --> 52:49.080
'RAMESH MARBLES'

52:49.959 --> 52:51.958
Are you gonnna get me beaten up
by the students

52:51.959 --> 52:54.609
for supporting your damned fest emotion?

52:54.811 --> 52:56.165
Swathi, it is a simple crisis.

52:56.710 --> 52:57.870
I will manage.

52:58.065 --> 53:00.207
<i>Next up, a song dedicated to
convener Samkutty</i>

53:00.208 --> 53:02.876
<i>by an admirer from 3rd year EC.</i>

53:02.877 --> 53:04.163
<i>Let's listen to that song.</i>

53:04.164 --> 53:08.803
<i>♪ My lover, mon amour ♪</i>

53:08.804 --> 53:12.524
<i>♪ My secret companion ♪</i>

53:13.367 --> 53:21.264
<i>♪ Lend an ear to
My tiny little wishes, my love ♪</i>

53:21.823 --> 53:25.143
<i>♪ Give me this same intense hold ♪</i>

53:26.377 --> 53:29.253
<i>♪ This same tight embrace ♪</i>

53:29.401 --> 53:31.474
Dude!

53:34.212 --> 53:37.010
Bro, mind if I flex a little now?

53:37.011 --> 53:37.947
Not at all, dude.

53:37.948 --> 53:40.413
You've been breaking your back
for this fest for 3 years!

53:40.414 --> 53:41.835
Time for some goddamn cheap mass show.

53:41.836 --> 53:43.085
Okay!

53:43.086 --> 53:44.513
♪ Aero my Dad's
Per annum my Dad's ♪

53:44.514 --> 53:45.881
Passing it to the convener.
One minute.

53:46.241 --> 53:47.375
Approved!

53:47.469 --> 53:49.066
<i>♪ Stardom my Dad's
PayTm my Dad's ♪</i>

53:49.067 --> 53:51.292
Passing it to the convener.
Hold on.

53:51.293 --> 53:53.012
- Move aside! Clear the way!
- Approved.

53:53.013 --> 53:55.643
<i>♪ Swirl and sway on the tail
Tripping and twirling like the rail ♪</i>

53:55.644 --> 53:57.257
- Water?
- Yeah, give me!

53:57.396 --> 53:58.356
Drone!

53:58.357 --> 54:00.889
<i>♪ Tripping and twirling like the rail ♪</i>

54:00.890 --> 54:02.485
<i>♪ Swirl and sway on the tail ♪</i>

54:02.486 --> 54:03.944
<i>♪ Cheap show!
Brief show! ♪</i>

54:03.945 --> 54:05.177
<i>♪ In between a petty show ♪</i>

54:05.178 --> 54:06.755
- How dare he...
- No! Don't!

54:06.756 --> 54:09.208
<i>♪ Altogether there's a fish show
Everyone's on the show ♪</i>

54:09.209 --> 54:10.426
Approved!

54:10.427 --> 54:12.885
<i>♪ Posts a DP wearing fake gold
And puts up a tacky show ♪</i>

54:14.698 --> 54:15.914
<i>♪ Cheap show ♪</i>

54:17.314 --> 54:18.461
<i>♪ Cheap show ♪</i>

54:19.934 --> 54:21.154
Yay!

54:22.264 --> 54:23.455
<i>♪ Cheap show ♪</i>

54:23.456 --> 54:25.532
<i>♪ Look at the beau! ♪</i>

54:25.533 --> 54:28.192
<i>♪ He's a helluva Showy-Man ♪</i>

54:28.193 --> 54:30.524
<i>♪ One classy 4K Shaw-some ♪</i>

54:30.525 --> 54:33.761
<i>♪ Watch!
His class act before the public! ♪</i>

54:33.762 --> 54:36.359
<i>♪ Honour my Dad's
Aero my Dad's ♪</i>

54:36.600 --> 54:37.685
Give me the knife, man!

54:37.686 --> 54:38.981
No, no!

54:40.041 --> 54:41.346
- What, man?
- JCB!

54:41.347 --> 54:42.617
Get to work!

54:42.618 --> 54:44.392
<i>♪ Stardom my Dad's
PayTm my Dad's ♪</i>

54:44.586 --> 54:46.001
- Will pass it to him.
- Approved.

54:46.002 --> 54:47.673
- Hey! Move!
- Stop it, man!

54:47.674 --> 54:49.689
<i>♪ Tripping and twirling like the rail ♪</i>

54:49.776 --> 54:51.103
Shall we put them in their place

54:51.197 --> 54:53.291
<i>♪ Swirl and sway on the tail!
Cheap show! ♪</i>

54:53.538 --> 54:55.224
Come on! Come forward!

54:56.996 --> 54:58.524
- One more 'approved' please.
- Approved.

54:58.947 --> 55:00.900
<i>♪ Tripping and twirling like the rail ♪</i>

55:01.692 --> 55:03.409
Hey boy. Step down.

55:03.410 --> 55:05.806
<i>♪ Swirl and sway on the tail ♪</i>

55:06.275 --> 55:07.392
<i>♪ Cheap show! ♪</i>

55:07.987 --> 55:09.016
- Weather okay?
- Okay.

55:09.017 --> 55:10.110
- Cars okay?
- Okay.

55:10.111 --> 55:11.490
- Bikes okay?
- Okay.

55:11.491 --> 55:12.716
Meghadoot?

55:12.717 --> 55:13.838
Guys!

55:15.312 --> 55:16.332
Kick off the rally!

55:35.031 --> 55:36.768
"Mamalassery Temple
Thrikkodiyettu Procession"

55:36.769 --> 55:38.855
- Agni, your herbal water.
- Hands off me!

56:35.116 --> 56:36.736
BCET!

56:36.869 --> 56:38.616
Long live, BCET!

56:38.957 --> 56:40.971
All hail BCET!

56:41.097 --> 56:42.723
Kuttan bro!

56:43.106 --> 56:44.730
Hey! What are you guys doing here?

56:44.731 --> 56:46.239
There's a mud race here tomorrow.

56:46.455 --> 56:48.692
First prize is 80,000 rupees.
We came to check it out.

56:48.693 --> 56:49.692
80,000 rupees?

56:49.693 --> 56:50.752
Yeah. Wanna join, bro?

56:50.753 --> 56:52.228
Even outsiders can compete.

56:52.522 --> 56:54.566
Come on, bro. Give it a shot.

56:54.567 --> 56:55.666
Get lost, man.

56:55.667 --> 56:58.086
See you in the evening. Okay.

57:09.304 --> 57:10.550
Clap your hands!

57:11.753 --> 57:13.173
Clap your hands, dude!

57:14.170 --> 57:15.376
Big round of applause!

57:18.720 --> 57:20.365
Lower the volume! Such a nuisance!

57:20.366 --> 57:22.744
- Looks like they're Gen-Z.
- So what? Aren’t they human?

57:27.609 --> 57:28.709
What is it? Huh?

57:28.916 --> 57:29.940
Get lost!

57:29.941 --> 57:31.280
- Can't you see a procession?
- So what?

57:31.281 --> 57:33.090
- Who are you?
- Trying to interrupt it?

57:33.091 --> 57:34.191
Get lost!

57:34.192 --> 57:35.617
Who are you? Get outta here!

57:35.618 --> 57:37.206
What? Get lost!

57:38.743 --> 57:39.771
Get out of here!

57:39.772 --> 57:42.858
If those clowns show off here again,
I'll crack their skulls!

57:42.859 --> 57:44.905
- Let go. They're just kids.
- How long do we tolerate this?

57:44.906 --> 57:46.062
It's okay. Keep moving.

57:49.745 --> 57:51.877
- What happened? You okay?
- I feel dizzy.

57:51.878 --> 57:53.647
Do you have water?

57:53.648 --> 57:55.415
Did you transfer
Vineeth Sreenivasan's payment--

57:55.416 --> 57:57.497
Hey, get her some water.
She’s feeling dizzy.

57:57.498 --> 57:59.147
Water... Swathi...
I am the convener of the...

57:59.148 --> 58:00.334
She's not okay! Get water first!

58:00.335 --> 58:01.383
Okay. Okay.

58:01.637 --> 58:03.037
What a crisis!

58:03.941 --> 58:05.642
- Bro, got water?
- No, man!

58:07.844 --> 58:09.031
Give it fast!

58:10.420 --> 58:11.737
Dear, please give some water?

58:11.738 --> 58:12.800
An aunty needs it.

58:12.801 --> 58:14.175
- No, I won't!
- Please give it.

58:14.176 --> 58:15.096
No can do!

58:15.097 --> 58:16.724
- She’s dizzy and really thirsty.
- No way!

58:16.725 --> 58:18.557
- I just asked for water!
- I said no. Let go!

58:19.838 --> 58:21.924
How dare you touch
master's herbal water? Huh?

58:22.195 --> 58:23.800
- Oh, so you're the Master?
- Yeah, I am!

58:23.801 --> 58:25.497
- Get lost!
- I am sorry!

58:29.428 --> 58:31.079
How dare you touch Samkutty bro?

58:32.162 --> 58:33.162
Okay?

58:35.893 --> 58:37.792
Catch him! Come on!

58:37.793 --> 58:39.040
What is it, huh?

58:44.710 --> 58:45.909
Flash mob!

58:50.205 --> 58:51.478
Don't come! Stay back!

58:52.225 --> 58:54.231
Bro, wait! Don't come!

59:09.873 --> 59:12.006
<i>♪ No secrets between us ♪</i>

59:12.439 --> 59:14.872
<i>♪ Love without limits ♪</i>

59:15.360 --> 59:17.560
<i>♪ We will never part ways ♪</i>

59:18.007 --> 59:19.204
<i>♪ We are friends ♪</i>

59:19.205 --> 59:20.725
Are you making a fool out of us?

59:21.920 --> 59:23.100
Please don't!

59:23.726 --> 59:24.990
You guys making fools of us?

59:24.991 --> 59:26.407
Hey, Buddies! No!

59:27.754 --> 59:28.720
These guys...

59:34.921 --> 59:37.222
Wait, are they part of the flash mob too?

59:37.223 --> 59:38.247
Nope!

59:40.012 --> 59:41.046
Is this a real fight?

59:41.047 --> 59:42.104
Original!

59:42.105 --> 59:43.765
Oh no, a fight! Run!

59:44.446 --> 59:45.963
Son, this way! Escape!

59:45.964 --> 59:47.020
Run!

59:48.912 --> 59:51.024
Hey, stop! Please!

59:52.447 --> 59:54.521
The event’s done! Don’t hit me!
I’m the convener!

59:54.522 --> 59:56.205
Bloody villagers!

59:56.206 --> 59:57.328
Come on!

59:59.176 --> 01:00:00.343
Move! Move!

01:00:04.476 --> 01:00:05.560
My coat!

01:00:05.561 --> 01:00:07.011
My son's coat!

01:00:07.443 --> 01:00:09.561
Hey, aren't you guys
the discipline committee?

01:00:10.591 --> 01:00:12.551
Bunch of undisciplined clowns!

01:00:19.063 --> 01:00:20.197
Hit them all!

01:00:26.597 --> 01:00:28.324
Beat him up!

01:00:30.366 --> 01:00:32.128
Kuttan bro!

01:00:41.570 --> 01:00:43.217
Hey! Move!

01:00:50.814 --> 01:00:52.552
Hit him, hit him!

01:00:55.846 --> 01:00:57.142
Don't hit him!

01:00:58.226 --> 01:00:59.720
Hey, don't hit him!

01:01:03.577 --> 01:01:05.337
I said don't hit him!

01:01:12.984 --> 01:01:14.477
What a show-off!

01:01:17.337 --> 01:01:19.277
Dude, the controller is gone!

01:01:19.696 --> 01:01:22.430
It's moving! Do something!
Stop it!

01:01:22.431 --> 01:01:23.617
I'm coming.

01:01:23.618 --> 01:01:24.633
Clear off, you idiots!

01:01:26.616 --> 01:01:27.856
Bro, you okay?

01:01:32.827 --> 01:01:33.984
All okay?

01:01:34.212 --> 01:01:35.390
You alright?

01:01:46.002 --> 01:01:47.795
Oh, Mother Goddess of Mudippura!

01:02:11.814 --> 01:02:13.867
This is Arohan!

01:02:39.853 --> 01:02:42.152
<i>Good thing they stopped it in time.</i>

01:02:42.153 --> 01:02:44.650
There's a contusion on your foot bone.

01:02:44.651 --> 01:02:46.439
I've put a crepe bandage for now.

01:02:46.711 --> 01:02:49.886
If the pain stays after 7-8 days,

01:02:49.887 --> 01:02:52.424
come back for a review and
we'll do an X-ray.

01:02:52.425 --> 01:02:53.498
Okay, doctor.

01:02:53.625 --> 01:02:54.631
Okay.

01:03:05.115 --> 01:03:06.563
Scrolling Facebook now?

01:03:06.564 --> 01:03:07.681
There's a reason.

01:03:07.682 --> 01:03:08.730
Bro...

01:03:08.731 --> 01:03:10.133
I'll surrender, bro.

01:03:11.064 --> 01:03:12.291
Hidden gem, my foot!

01:03:13.828 --> 01:03:14.979
Guys...

01:03:14.980 --> 01:03:17.041
The cops won't touch the 'Koottukaar' gang!

01:03:17.042 --> 01:03:18.248
Now watch my mom's power!

01:03:19.005 --> 01:03:20.453
Bloody freaks!

01:03:21.588 --> 01:03:22.678
Advise your son.

01:03:22.679 --> 01:03:23.691
Mom, all sorted?

01:03:23.692 --> 01:03:25.388
Hey Chakki! How dare you fight on the road?

01:03:25.389 --> 01:03:26.421
Chakki?!

01:03:26.551 --> 01:03:28.285
- Let go of me, mom.
- You!

01:03:28.286 --> 01:03:29.767
He’s not Vivi… he’s a baby!

01:03:29.768 --> 01:03:31.301
My friends are watching, Mom!

01:03:31.302 --> 01:03:32.455
Two more, go on!

01:03:32.456 --> 01:03:34.935
- Please don't embarrass me!
- What's so funny, huh?

01:03:34.936 --> 01:03:36.845
Your butts should be set on fire!

01:03:36.846 --> 01:03:38.048
Come with me!

01:03:38.049 --> 01:03:40.994
Look at his fashion!
Good for nothing!

01:03:41.136 --> 01:03:43.209
Who else is in this
'Koottukaar, the buddies' gang?

01:03:43.877 --> 01:03:45.081
Not me. Not me.

01:03:45.082 --> 01:03:47.552
Wait, you guys don't even know
if you're buddies?

01:03:48.268 --> 01:03:49.441
- Saji...
- Sir?

01:03:49.696 --> 01:03:51.109
Call their parents here.

01:03:51.202 --> 01:03:52.266
And file an FIR.

01:03:52.267 --> 01:03:54.143
- Oh no. Please sir...
- Sorry, sir...

01:03:54.427 --> 01:03:56.679
Vineeth Sreenivasan's ProShow is tonight.

01:03:56.680 --> 01:03:58.417
Sir... please hear me out, sir...

01:03:59.651 --> 01:04:00.671
What do we do now?

01:04:03.904 --> 01:04:04.966
Bro...

01:04:04.967 --> 01:04:06.941
The situation is out of control.

01:04:07.551 --> 01:04:10.171
Whenever I call that guy,
some Tamil or Telugu starts playing!

01:04:10.378 --> 01:04:12.198
He even sent me a voice note.

01:04:12.778 --> 01:04:13.869
Just listen to this.

01:04:13.870 --> 01:04:15.952
<i>"Even nonsense has its limits."</i>

01:04:16.042 --> 01:04:19.429
<i>"If you can't conduct an event,
don't even try."</i>

01:04:19.691 --> 01:04:20.738
<i>"Have a good day."</i>

01:04:20.739 --> 01:04:22.052
There's a Hindi version too, listen.

01:04:22.053 --> 01:04:23.688
<i>'Nonsense karne ko bhi...'</i>

01:04:25.064 --> 01:04:27.964
The rest of the committee says
you're the one who caused this mess.

01:04:28.450 --> 01:04:30.550
That's what everyone is saying.

01:04:30.551 --> 01:04:34.858
They say this is fallout from
your old gang wars.

01:04:41.082 --> 01:04:42.255
We're screwed.

01:04:43.616 --> 01:04:44.763
Sir...

01:04:45.634 --> 01:04:50.507
Considering the heroics you pulled off
at SN College back in the day...

01:04:55.414 --> 01:04:58.460
This is something
you can easily understand, right?

01:04:59.796 --> 01:05:01.183
Right? Right?

01:05:01.498 --> 01:05:03.552
- Yes, yes.
- Yes.

01:05:03.553 --> 01:05:04.753
Yes.

01:05:06.646 --> 01:05:08.164
How do you know all that?

01:05:08.399 --> 01:05:10.226
Everyone in our college knows it.

01:05:10.857 --> 01:05:12.763
You're the local SI after all.

01:05:13.073 --> 01:05:16.429
The tales of you single-handedly gheraoing
Ashram Road,

01:05:16.430 --> 01:05:17.631
everybody knows that.

01:05:17.632 --> 01:05:18.704
- Right?
- Yes, yes.

01:05:23.234 --> 01:05:25.963
- And that overnight evacuation...
- No, it didn’t work out.

01:05:26.843 --> 01:05:29.826
Since the guys you beat up haven't filed
a complaint, you may leave now.

01:05:29.827 --> 01:05:32.038
But if this happens again,
you'll see my real face.

01:05:32.607 --> 01:05:33.651
Get going.

01:05:33.652 --> 01:05:35.314
I knew from the start

01:05:35.315 --> 01:05:37.003
this would end exactly like this.

01:05:37.004 --> 01:05:39.354
Coming here itself was a waste.

01:05:39.355 --> 01:05:42.727
No matter how hard you try to be decent...

01:05:42.728 --> 01:05:46.534
your sins will always come chasing you!

01:05:47.037 --> 01:05:49.982
One day he'll die by someone's knife!

01:05:49.983 --> 01:05:52.030
Hey, stop talking rubbish!

01:05:52.197 --> 01:05:54.234
You saw the college kids storming in,
didn't you?

01:05:54.889 --> 01:05:56.974
Even with all this trouble,
did he raise his hand?

01:05:59.272 --> 01:06:01.379
Look how calm he's standing even now.

01:06:09.748 --> 01:06:10.792
Sir!

01:06:10.793 --> 01:06:12.553
Calm, my foot!

01:06:13.293 --> 01:06:15.142
Back in the day,
he used those hands a lot.

01:06:15.143 --> 01:06:17.515
Now when it's actually needed,
he's suddenly calm!

01:06:17.516 --> 01:06:18.568
Sir...

01:06:18.569 --> 01:06:20.441
There's a problem.
The guy they beat up is...

01:06:21.983 --> 01:06:24.090
That's exactly why you ended up like this.

01:06:24.509 --> 01:06:26.496
Don't make me start again.

01:06:28.263 --> 01:06:29.707
You sure? Is it him?

01:06:29.708 --> 01:06:31.112
It's Kuttan, sir. Look.

01:06:31.888 --> 01:06:33.455
Hey, hey! Wait!

01:06:36.005 --> 01:06:37.898
You guys beat up Kuttan?

01:06:38.102 --> 01:06:41.742
You picked a fight with Thotta Kuttan,
you senseless idiots?

01:06:51.446 --> 01:06:53.037
Oh no! Thotta Kuttan?

01:06:54.690 --> 01:06:55.748
Who is he?

01:06:55.749 --> 01:06:57.234
Whoever it is,
we're cooked for sure!

01:06:57.235 --> 01:06:59.371
You think he's someone
you can casually mess with?

01:06:59.494 --> 01:07:01.161
He's a criminal! A full-on criminal!

01:07:05.480 --> 01:07:07.140
Did you see my knife?

01:07:09.597 --> 01:07:11.790
Sir, isn't he some random singer guy?

01:07:12.546 --> 01:07:13.942
Thirty men came to finish him.

01:07:13.943 --> 01:07:16.456
So he rammed them into
the Thuckalay rocks with a jeep

01:07:16.457 --> 01:07:17.938
and blasted them with thotta bomb!

01:07:17.939 --> 01:07:19.655
That "singer" of yours did that!

01:07:19.656 --> 01:07:20.921
You know Appalam Haji,

01:07:20.922 --> 01:07:23.671
the guy who rules loading and parking
at Chala Market?

01:07:23.965 --> 01:07:27.589
That uncle from the goonda list
who pops up in newspapers sometimes?

01:07:27.590 --> 01:07:28.794
Yeah, that same uncle.

01:07:28.795 --> 01:07:31.555
Kuttan stabbed a loading hook
through that uncle's chest

01:07:31.556 --> 01:07:33.149
and ripped flesh out!

01:07:33.676 --> 01:07:35.226
And that too on a busy market day.

01:07:35.227 --> 01:07:37.220
Plus 7 other cases of
attacking with thotta bombs.

01:07:37.221 --> 01:07:39.147
Back then, he played
with bombs and explosives.

01:07:39.148 --> 01:07:41.545
Now he wears a sacred thread
like Velayudhan from Naran,

01:07:41.546 --> 01:07:43.521
and walks the path of music and family.

01:07:43.680 --> 01:07:45.022
He's a goonda!

01:07:45.023 --> 01:07:46.358
A damn singing goonda!

01:07:49.202 --> 01:07:51.062
If he ever takes off that sacred thread...

01:08:00.178 --> 01:08:02.831
<i>♪ You are the supreme lord
The ever-raging force ♪</i>

01:08:03.111 --> 01:08:05.584
<i>♪ To the ultimate foe
You are the ultimate terror ♪</i>

01:08:05.699 --> 01:08:08.029
<i>♪ To the fierce Kali
You are the reigning master ♪</i>

01:08:08.030 --> 01:08:10.942
<i>♪ The Ocean God's blazing arrow! ♪</i>

01:08:10.943 --> 01:08:13.209
<i>♪ A violent storm, a raging cyclone! ♪</i>

01:08:13.519 --> 01:08:15.786
<i>♪ The dark ruler, the crushing force ♪</i>

01:08:15.994 --> 01:08:18.380
<i>♪ The bringer of fury
The devastating plague! ♪</i>

01:08:21.388 --> 01:08:23.522
- Dude, that Kuttan...
- Relax. No issue.

01:08:23.840 --> 01:08:26.553
He's a retired goon, man.
Even if he tries, nothing's gonna happen.

01:08:29.788 --> 01:08:31.382
No way!

01:08:44.636 --> 01:08:45.803
Bro! Bro!

01:08:46.759 --> 01:08:49.555
We're from the treasure hunt.
Traditional dhoti and a flashy outfit.

01:08:49.556 --> 01:08:51.669
The answer is Mangifera indica.
Clue, please?

01:08:52.047 --> 01:08:53.068
Dude, it's not them!

01:08:53.069 --> 01:08:54.507
No time to waste. Clue please!

01:08:54.508 --> 01:08:55.508
Give him the clue.

01:08:56.283 --> 01:08:57.376
Clue?

01:08:57.614 --> 01:08:58.754
Oh, my!

01:09:01.990 --> 01:09:03.977
Who's got the guts to step in here?

01:09:17.253 --> 01:09:19.750
<i>♪ Sa... Serpent-headed, subduer of all! ♪</i>

01:09:19.751 --> 01:09:22.403
<i>♪ Ri... Ruin of foes, the fierce Rudra! ♪</i>

01:09:22.404 --> 01:09:24.947
<i>♪ Ga... Great and soaring,
The majestic Garuda! ♪</i>

01:09:24.948 --> 01:09:27.350
<i>♪ Ma... Master of the apocalypse,
The mighty hunter! ♪</i>

01:09:27.351 --> 01:09:28.665
Bro, don't! That's not our car!

01:09:28.666 --> 01:09:29.672
Let go!

01:09:33.776 --> 01:09:36.087
Please don't! It's Dennichan's car...
it’ll be trouble!

01:10:01.436 --> 01:10:04.069
<i>♪ Like Karna, Kalki, and Kama ♪</i>

01:10:04.376 --> 01:10:06.662
<i>♪ The destroyer of Kamsa and Keechaka ♪</i>

01:10:06.979 --> 01:10:09.285
<i>♪ The Ekalavya of this world ♪</i>

01:10:09.785 --> 01:10:11.892
<i>♪ Forged with the strength
of eight metals! ♪</i>

01:10:12.256 --> 01:10:14.780
<i>♪ Protector of the aeons,
Master of mystic arts ♪</i>

01:10:14.781 --> 01:10:17.413
<i>♪ The fierce warrior of Rudra! ♪</i>

01:10:17.414 --> 01:10:19.418
<i>♪ Conqueror of lust, wrath,
Delusion, and greed ♪</i>

01:10:19.419 --> 01:10:22.713
<i>♪ The lone hero, lord of Lanka,
Bathed in the blood of Gods and Demons ♪</i>

01:10:22.714 --> 01:10:25.554
<i>♪ You are the dawn of the apocalypse! ♪</i>

01:10:27.476 --> 01:10:29.333
Dude, he came, flexed,
and now leaving!

01:10:29.334 --> 01:10:30.514
You put on some show now!

01:10:30.796 --> 01:10:31.827
What show?

01:10:31.828 --> 01:10:33.203
Do something!

01:11:12.464 --> 01:11:14.636
Did you hear about the fight
that happened in college, Father?

01:11:14.637 --> 01:11:16.785
- A fight?
- The one near the front gate!

01:11:17.215 --> 01:11:18.291
That was a street play!

01:11:18.292 --> 01:11:20.776
- A social awareness street play.
- No, a literal street fight!

01:11:20.777 --> 01:11:22.492
Hey, nothing serious.

01:11:22.588 --> 01:11:25.807
Sanal sir just wanted
a quick word with Samkutty.

01:11:25.808 --> 01:11:28.082
That’s all this meeting is about.
Nothing else...

01:11:28.083 --> 01:11:29.027
Absolutely nothing!

01:11:29.028 --> 01:11:31.238
Hey Sam, come to my room.

01:11:37.581 --> 01:11:38.550
Cheers, bro.

01:11:38.551 --> 01:11:39.598
Hey, Sam’s here.

01:11:39.599 --> 01:11:41.338
- So, what happened?
- Kind of a scene.

01:11:41.339 --> 01:11:43.088
Lovely madam wasn’t agreeing at first.

01:11:43.089 --> 01:11:45.557
Since Kuttan and his gang
trashed the campus,

01:11:45.558 --> 01:11:47.518
the management wants to file a complaint.

01:11:47.519 --> 01:11:48.612
Ah, okay.

01:11:48.613 --> 01:11:51.043
Right now they’re letting it slide

01:11:51.044 --> 01:11:53.486
only because Vineeth Sreenivasan’s show
is sold out.

01:11:53.487 --> 01:11:56.596
But if one more issue pops up,
the fest is definitely cancelled.

01:11:57.041 --> 01:11:58.073
Bro, then--

01:11:58.074 --> 01:12:00.489
Swathi! Swathi! Sorry guys,
CET students are calling.

01:12:00.490 --> 01:12:02.983
You have to come to the green room.
Come. Quick.

01:12:02.984 --> 01:12:05.175
We sent them for collections,
not a single shop paid.

01:12:05.176 --> 01:12:08.052
Kuttan and his gang told everyone
not to donate.

01:12:08.308 --> 01:12:09.316
Samkutty…

01:12:09.550 --> 01:12:11.317
Something’s brewing.

01:12:11.604 --> 01:12:13.408
We’ll handle things inside campus.

01:12:13.409 --> 01:12:15.329
We’ve placed volunteers
at the back gate too.

01:12:15.441 --> 01:12:16.449
How’s that?

01:12:19.080 --> 01:12:20.245
You do absolutely nothing.

01:12:20.246 --> 01:12:22.135
Just go grab an ice cream and chill.

01:12:22.136 --> 01:12:23.143
Okay, bro.

01:12:23.144 --> 01:12:25.571
Not just campus.
Cover the FM lab too.

01:12:25.572 --> 01:12:26.848
And the parking area.

01:12:26.849 --> 01:12:28.270
We need eyes everywhere.

01:12:28.271 --> 01:12:30.275
So no drinking tonight.

01:12:30.276 --> 01:12:31.518
Never, bro.

01:12:31.841 --> 01:12:33.106
Shh... don’t throw it away!

01:12:33.737 --> 01:12:35.533
It’s not as easy as you think.

01:12:35.534 --> 01:12:37.020
That guy’s a certified OG terror.

01:12:37.394 --> 01:12:39.110
So I’ve set up a little plan.

01:12:39.111 --> 01:12:40.074
What plan?

01:12:40.075 --> 01:12:41.828
Hired a few goons from Muttathara.

01:12:41.829 --> 01:12:43.416
Clash Madhu, Kattappa Suni.

01:12:43.417 --> 01:12:45.167
Both are Kuttan’s equal rivals.

01:12:45.168 --> 01:12:46.275
Look...

01:12:46.276 --> 01:12:47.403
I don’t want any soft drink.

01:12:49.854 --> 01:12:50.862
Hey! What’s this?

01:12:50.956 --> 01:12:52.276
You take our money and mock us?

01:12:52.277 --> 01:12:53.407
You loser!

01:12:53.408 --> 01:12:54.893
I’ll handle this crisis myself.

01:12:54.894 --> 01:12:56.174
Yeah, you better.

01:12:56.175 --> 01:12:58.390
When Vineeth Sreenivasan arrives,
there should be zero drama.

01:12:58.391 --> 01:12:59.873
If he sees a mess,
it’ll look bad.

01:12:59.874 --> 01:13:00.959
Very bad. Really bad.

01:13:00.960 --> 01:13:02.464
To hell with his ice cream!

01:13:05.168 --> 01:13:06.682
- Is there booze in it
- Yeah.

01:13:06.910 --> 01:13:07.918
I’ll need it.

01:13:08.363 --> 01:13:09.556
Go straight and take a right.

01:13:09.557 --> 01:13:10.987
Kavya, what about the CET guys?

01:13:10.988 --> 01:13:12.299
- All sorted.
- It’s all sorted.

01:13:12.300 --> 01:13:13.729
- Okay.
- We’ve handled everything.

01:13:13.730 --> 01:13:15.559
Samkutty, I’ve made those corrections.

01:13:15.560 --> 01:13:16.614
Yeah, that works.

01:13:16.863 --> 01:13:18.839
Take it to the LED and run a test.

01:13:24.347 --> 01:13:25.658
Will your brother come tomorrow?

01:13:26.892 --> 01:13:28.642
Nothing’s finalized yet.

01:13:28.838 --> 01:13:30.385
I’ve pulled a small trick.

01:13:34.621 --> 01:13:35.667
- Hello.
- Hello.

01:13:35.668 --> 01:13:36.917
Joseph, right?

01:13:36.918 --> 01:13:38.408
Yes. Who’s this?

01:13:39.410 --> 01:13:40.861
This is Merin’s father.

01:13:41.387 --> 01:13:42.394
Wilson.

01:13:43.488 --> 01:13:44.635
Ah... yes.

01:13:44.636 --> 01:13:45.775
Where are you now?

01:13:45.776 --> 01:13:46.970
<i>Are you in town?</i>

01:13:47.089 --> 01:13:48.640
I... I’m in Thoothukudi.

01:13:48.641 --> 01:13:49.859
I work here.

01:13:49.860 --> 01:13:50.868
Oh.

01:13:51.445 --> 01:13:52.904
Nothing else.

01:13:53.162 --> 01:13:54.504
Got a call from college.

01:13:55.538 --> 01:13:57.765
They’re hosting the fest this time.

01:13:58.335 --> 01:14:00.865
<i>So… Merin’s old magazine...</i>

01:14:01.170 --> 01:14:03.537
<i>The students said
they’re finally releasing it.</i>

01:14:04.035 --> 01:14:05.589
I thought...

01:14:06.097 --> 01:14:08.308
it would be nice
if you could come too, Joseph.

01:14:09.809 --> 01:14:12.503
I... there’s no one else at the site...

01:14:12.504 --> 01:14:13.409
<i>So...</i>

01:14:13.410 --> 01:14:15.594
<i>I... not sure...</i>

01:14:15.807 --> 01:14:17.307
Well... I mean...

01:14:18.845 --> 01:14:20.180
Joseph, you must come.

01:14:20.619 --> 01:14:21.627
I...

01:14:26.854 --> 01:14:28.766
You like your brother that much?

01:14:29.340 --> 01:14:30.620
Of course!

01:14:30.621 --> 01:14:31.963
He’s amazing.

01:14:32.770 --> 01:14:36.377
You know those perfect,
goody-goody guys we see around?

01:14:36.939 --> 01:14:39.323
They usually have
some top-tier shady business going on.

01:14:39.324 --> 01:14:40.604
But he’s not like that.

01:14:40.605 --> 01:14:43.119
Inside and out,
he’s genuinely a good guy.

01:14:47.040 --> 01:14:48.048
Vodka. Want some?

01:14:48.289 --> 01:14:49.297
No.

01:14:51.110 --> 01:14:52.483
So, my brother...

01:14:53.186 --> 01:14:56.584
When I was around seven,
our mom left us.

01:14:57.149 --> 01:14:58.157
Oh.

01:14:58.329 --> 01:14:59.337
Hey... sorry.

01:14:59.547 --> 01:15:02.000
Did she have some health issue?

01:15:02.001 --> 01:15:03.017
No.

01:15:03.018 --> 01:15:05.431
She literally left us...
eloped with someone.

01:15:07.157 --> 01:15:09.227
We never really knew the exact reason.

01:15:09.547 --> 01:15:11.633
Dad used to drink a lot back then.

01:15:20.126 --> 01:15:22.429
Maybe mom had her own logic.

01:15:23.016 --> 01:15:24.414
- But mom...
- Samkutty, got a pen?

01:15:24.415 --> 01:15:25.422
Yes.

01:15:27.040 --> 01:15:30.110
After mom left,
dad’s life sort of crashed.

01:15:31.045 --> 01:15:34.122
Honestly, it was my 11 year old brother
who took care of me.

01:15:34.398 --> 01:15:37.008
He restored some balance at home.

01:15:37.344 --> 01:15:41.094
After that, Dad started
trying harder to be a better father.

01:15:41.803 --> 01:15:43.704
Even though it was just
three guys at home...

01:15:43.705 --> 01:15:44.779
we were happy.

01:15:46.313 --> 01:15:48.867
But after my brother left,
nothing feels right.

01:15:48.977 --> 01:15:51.651
Life’s like a boring government ad now.

01:15:52.675 --> 01:15:55.237
And I’ve always been a spoiled brat
for my dad anyway.

01:16:00.233 --> 01:16:03.089
If my brother comes for this fest...

01:16:03.379 --> 01:16:05.039
meets everyone

01:16:05.337 --> 01:16:07.063
and faces all this again...

01:16:07.396 --> 01:16:09.193
maybe... things might click again.

01:16:11.445 --> 01:16:13.147
Everything might be okay again.

01:16:15.181 --> 01:16:16.188
Sam...

01:16:17.374 --> 01:16:18.778
Do you need a hug?

01:16:22.085 --> 01:16:24.014
Hey! Get lost!

01:16:27.313 --> 01:16:28.321
Or maybe a...

01:16:30.144 --> 01:16:31.275
Swathi, are you crying?

01:16:31.276 --> 01:16:33.375
What? Why would I cry?

01:16:35.627 --> 01:16:38.220
Swathi, you don’t cry easily either,
just like me, right?

01:16:40.427 --> 01:16:42.713
Everything will be fine.
The event will be awesome.

01:16:42.714 --> 01:16:44.321
Your brother will come tomorrow too.

01:16:44.733 --> 01:16:46.435
So all okay, right?

01:16:46.824 --> 01:16:48.512
You’ve lost your muscles now.

01:16:49.702 --> 01:16:50.934
No motivation anymore.

01:16:51.989 --> 01:16:53.450
Who am I even trying to impress?

01:16:56.084 --> 01:16:58.114
By the way,
when is Vineeth Sreenivasan arriving?

01:16:58.811 --> 01:17:01.494
Vineethettan’s
on the 8 a.m. flight tomorrow.

01:17:01.675 --> 01:17:07.042
<i>♪ Your face, like a radiant white moon ♪</i>

01:17:07.715 --> 01:17:13.597
<i>♪ Lights up the dark blue sky ♪</i>

01:17:13.598 --> 01:17:18.348
<i>♪ Your face, like a radiant white moon ♪</i>

01:17:19.434 --> 01:17:22.256
<i>♪ Your face, like a radiant white moon ♪</i>

01:17:22.257 --> 01:17:23.265
Bro!

01:17:24.522 --> 01:17:25.786
- Bro!
- Bro!

01:17:27.505 --> 01:17:28.693
What are you doing here?

01:17:28.694 --> 01:17:30.600
Got a college show here.
What about you?

01:17:30.601 --> 01:17:31.896
An award function.

01:17:31.897 --> 01:17:33.975
Universal music director
Shaan Rahman!

01:17:33.976 --> 01:17:35.382
At Sreemoolam Club.

01:17:35.562 --> 01:17:37.068
Come along. I’ll drop you.

01:17:37.968 --> 01:17:40.115
Hey, they’ve arranged
biriyani for me there.

01:17:40.116 --> 01:17:43.029
I’ll get you biriyani.
I’m dropping you!

01:17:43.030 --> 01:17:44.594
Be honest.
Came to give the award?

01:17:44.595 --> 01:17:45.742
No man, seriously...

01:17:47.093 --> 01:17:49.131
Dude, it’s been a while.
Where is he?

01:17:50.108 --> 01:17:51.116
Yeah, true.

01:17:54.484 --> 01:17:57.335
Bro, Vineethettan’s flight
hasn’t landed yet.

01:17:57.422 --> 01:17:59.432
What? He texted me he already landed.

01:17:59.433 --> 01:18:00.972
Where are you guys?

01:18:00.973 --> 01:18:03.103
We’re right in front
of the Domestic Terminal.

01:18:03.104 --> 01:18:04.367
What? Domestic?!

01:18:04.368 --> 01:18:05.807
Not domestic, International!

01:18:05.808 --> 01:18:07.366
- Go pick him up fast, okay?
- International?!

01:18:07.367 --> 01:18:08.366
Ah, okay, okay.

01:18:08.367 --> 01:18:10.003
International!
International! International!

01:18:10.004 --> 01:18:11.484
Bro, the other side of the airport!

01:18:11.485 --> 01:18:13.944
- The other side? Why?
- Come on, move, move!

01:18:18.309 --> 01:18:20.112
Now I’m totally confused.

01:18:20.356 --> 01:18:22.535
Why’d he land there?
Isn’t Domestic this side?

01:18:22.864 --> 01:18:24.169
How would I know?

01:18:24.170 --> 01:18:26.256
- I’ve never even been on a flight.
- Domestic... International...

01:18:26.257 --> 01:18:28.652
Hey, I think
I just saw Vineeth Sreenivasan.

01:18:29.155 --> 01:18:31.677
We’re going to pick him up,
and you say you saw him already?

01:18:32.889 --> 01:18:34.169
Nah...

01:18:34.170 --> 01:18:35.481
Must’ve been someone else.

01:18:36.076 --> 01:18:37.520
Manager’s calling.

01:18:37.521 --> 01:18:38.779
- Pick it up.
- Yeah, bro.

01:18:39.233 --> 01:18:41.764
Ah, Samkutty,
glad you picked up Vineethettan.

01:18:41.874 --> 01:18:45.116
- Picked up?!
- <i>Drop him at the hotel, okay?</i>

01:18:45.117 --> 01:18:46.187
Okay.

01:18:47.371 --> 01:18:49.424
- What happened?
- Vineethettan has already been picked up.

01:18:49.425 --> 01:18:50.508
Picked up?

01:18:50.509 --> 01:18:51.531
- Who?
- Who?

01:18:57.368 --> 01:18:59.195
You must be college professors, right?

01:18:59.479 --> 01:19:00.761
Yes, yes.

01:19:00.762 --> 01:19:02.404
This is Professor Subhash Paul.

01:19:02.405 --> 01:19:03.715
I’m Manik Pasha.

01:19:03.811 --> 01:19:04.819
Oh.

01:19:05.459 --> 01:19:08.083
I think Kuttan Goonda was driving that car!

01:19:08.265 --> 01:19:09.646
- Kuttan? -Yeah.
- Kuttan?!

01:19:12.412 --> 01:19:13.645
- KIDNAP!!!
- KIDNAP!!!

01:19:13.646 --> 01:19:15.014
U-turn! U-turn! U-turn!

01:19:15.015 --> 01:19:16.732
Which branch? Mechanical?

01:19:16.887 --> 01:19:18.530
Yeah, yeah. Mechanical.

01:19:18.531 --> 01:19:19.725
Me, brake and clutch,

01:19:19.849 --> 01:19:23.061
and bro... I mean, Subhash sir...
carburetor and valve.

01:19:23.178 --> 01:19:25.241
And we... oil change!

01:19:32.319 --> 01:19:33.468
<i>Vineethetta!</i>

01:19:33.469 --> 01:19:34.743
<i>Vineeth sir!!!</i>

01:19:34.744 --> 01:19:36.095
<i>- Vineethetta!
- Look here! Behind!</i>

01:19:36.096 --> 01:19:38.766
- Bro, they’re chasing us!
- <i>-Hey! Look here, Vineeth sir!</i>

01:19:39.182 --> 01:19:40.891
Stop the car, bro!

01:19:40.892 --> 01:19:42.463
- Vineeth sir!
- Will see to it.

01:19:42.729 --> 01:19:43.862
Oh no!

01:19:49.186 --> 01:19:50.583
Vineethettaaaa!

01:19:50.584 --> 01:19:52.388
Look here,
your bouquet is in this car, mister!

01:19:52.389 --> 01:19:53.982
Hey, man, Vineethettaa...
Vineeth Sreenivasan!

01:19:53.983 --> 01:19:55.140
This is Arohan! This is Arohan!

01:19:55.141 --> 01:19:57.338
- Vineethetta!
- This car! This car!

01:19:57.339 --> 01:20:00.218
Ozin, drive fast!
Samkutty, pull your leg inside!

01:20:00.219 --> 01:20:01.736
Hey, head inside!

01:20:01.737 --> 01:20:04.330
Hey, pull over!
Go fast!

01:20:04.331 --> 01:20:06.222
Vineethettan... Vineethettan...
He's a goonda!

01:20:06.813 --> 01:20:08.188
Not that car,

01:20:08.189 --> 01:20:09.477
this car!

01:20:09.478 --> 01:20:10.993
- This car! This car!
- Vineeth sir!

01:20:10.994 --> 01:20:12.102
Vineeth sir!

01:20:12.103 --> 01:20:13.631
This car, Vineethettaa!

01:20:13.632 --> 01:20:15.218
Parallel! Pull the car alongside!

01:20:15.219 --> 01:20:17.595
- Ozin, step on it!
- Vineethetta, Vineethetta...

01:20:17.596 --> 01:20:18.688
Sir!

01:20:20.222 --> 01:20:21.913
- That’s not it, you idiot!
- See.

01:20:21.914 --> 01:20:23.631
Fans have surrounded us. Drive faster!

01:20:23.632 --> 01:20:24.996
- Hey... hey...
- Hey, mister, look here!

01:20:24.997 --> 01:20:26.989
- You... kid... nap!
- Enough your dumb charades!

01:20:26.990 --> 01:20:29.410
Kids are sleeping.
They are in Chennai! Chennai!

01:20:29.411 --> 01:20:30.855
Ozin, cut across and block him!

01:20:30.856 --> 01:20:32.551
Move forward! Move forward!

01:20:33.061 --> 01:20:35.170
You... are... kidnapped!

01:20:35.493 --> 01:20:37.493
- You kidnapped!
- Read it, man! It's in English!

01:20:37.494 --> 01:20:39.394
Idiot, can't you read?!

01:20:39.395 --> 01:20:40.551
Go past the car.

01:20:45.202 --> 01:20:46.973
Vineethetta... hey...

01:20:50.787 --> 01:20:51.943
So...

01:20:52.280 --> 01:20:53.960
where’s our stay arranged?

01:20:54.867 --> 01:20:56.258
At Govinda Tourist Home, nearby.

01:20:56.345 --> 01:20:57.688
What the...!

01:21:00.150 --> 01:21:01.158
It's air-conditioned!

01:21:11.095 --> 01:21:12.837
Wrong car! Wrong car!

01:21:12.838 --> 01:21:14.818
Call the police! Call the police!

01:21:21.272 --> 01:21:22.584
- Hello?
- Hello.

01:21:22.585 --> 01:21:23.593
Police station?

01:21:24.019 --> 01:21:25.979
This is actor-director Vineeth Sreenivasan.

01:21:28.847 --> 01:21:29.855
Yes, sir?

01:21:31.307 --> 01:21:32.315
Hello, sir?

01:21:34.152 --> 01:21:35.705
<i>Sir, I can hear you.</i>

01:21:36.542 --> 01:21:37.971
Sir, are you the SI?

01:21:38.082 --> 01:21:39.090
Yes.

01:21:39.941 --> 01:21:41.401
What’s your name, sir?

01:21:41.555 --> 01:21:42.589
Manichan.

01:21:43.183 --> 01:21:44.667
Sir, you’re a top-class SI.

01:21:45.385 --> 01:21:46.940
I just called to introduce myself.

01:21:46.941 --> 01:21:49.769
Sir, you’re an absolute pride
of the Kerala Police Department.

01:21:49.972 --> 01:21:51.401
Okay, okay.

01:21:54.439 --> 01:21:56.047
What did you idiots think,

01:21:56.048 --> 01:21:57.572
you could just kidnap us?

01:21:57.722 --> 01:21:59.175
Forget him.

01:21:59.457 --> 01:22:00.737
Do you even know who I am?

01:22:00.839 --> 01:22:02.173
Kerala will literally burn!

01:22:02.590 --> 01:22:03.980
Who the hell are you guys?

01:22:08.174 --> 01:22:10.713
- Aaaarghhhhh!
- Oh my God!!!

01:22:13.738 --> 01:22:15.644
Hey. I’m Kuttan.

01:22:16.293 --> 01:22:17.753
They call me Thotta Kuttan.

01:22:18.652 --> 01:22:20.550
My last thotta explosion case happened

01:22:20.551 --> 01:22:22.456
because they denied me papad at a wedding!

01:22:22.925 --> 01:22:24.996
I burned down the entire kitchen!

01:22:25.925 --> 01:22:29.525
Once I lose it, I don’t care
if you’re a star or an astronaut,

01:22:29.620 --> 01:22:31.150
I’ll smash you!

01:22:32.549 --> 01:22:33.956
This is kidnapping!

01:22:33.957 --> 01:22:35.471
An honest kidnapping!

01:22:35.472 --> 01:22:36.480
Got it?!

01:22:40.758 --> 01:22:42.420
Vineethetta, I’m Samkutty.

01:22:42.421 --> 01:22:44.398
The convener of Arohan Fest.

01:22:45.758 --> 01:22:46.766
Huh?! Shaan ikka!

01:22:52.796 --> 01:22:53.804
Hey!

01:22:54.102 --> 01:22:56.461
I’m charging in
like a truck with no brakes!

01:22:57.157 --> 01:22:59.672
Don’t stand in the road
like a clueless puny frog.

01:22:59.805 --> 01:23:01.344
You’ll be dead meat! Okay?!

01:23:07.851 --> 01:23:08.859
Vineethetta...

01:23:09.779 --> 01:23:10.840
Stop!

01:23:10.841 --> 01:23:12.004
Stop the car, you!

01:23:12.349 --> 01:23:13.654
- Hey Samkutty...
- Sam...

01:23:14.038 --> 01:23:15.911
Ozin... Ozin... hurry!
Start the car!

01:23:15.912 --> 01:23:17.091
Come on!

01:23:27.064 --> 01:23:28.071
Brother...

01:23:28.901 --> 01:23:29.909
Samkutty...

01:23:30.604 --> 01:23:32.042
I’m coming to the college.

01:23:32.878 --> 01:23:34.119
Will reach by evening.

01:23:43.167 --> 01:23:45.236
Sir, look at this.

01:23:45.580 --> 01:23:47.533
- Directing, singing, all of it, right?
- Yes.

01:23:47.629 --> 01:23:51.142
On the occasion of
the Mamalassery Kavu Thrikkodiyettu Festival,

01:23:51.143 --> 01:23:52.705
I’ll be performing live tonight

01:23:52.808 --> 01:23:54.455
at 8 PM at the musical concert.

01:23:55.019 --> 01:23:56.480
And I’ll be there too.

01:23:56.481 --> 01:23:57.536
Some AI thing maybe...

01:23:57.537 --> 01:23:58.553
- Hey Saji.
- Yes, sir.

01:23:58.554 --> 01:24:00.132
Probably an AI video, sir.

01:24:01.118 --> 01:24:04.063
Hey, did Vineeth Sreenivasan
direct 'Jacobinte Swargarajyam?'

01:24:04.805 --> 01:24:06.649
Jacobinte Swargarajyam?

01:24:07.370 --> 01:24:08.378
Yes sir.

01:24:09.260 --> 01:24:11.495
If a guy like him calls
just to introduce himself,

01:24:11.496 --> 01:24:13.120
that’s a big deal, right?

01:24:13.121 --> 01:24:14.153
Of course!

01:24:14.154 --> 01:24:15.752
He’s a very busy man.

01:24:16.291 --> 01:24:17.447
Why do you ask, sir?

01:24:17.448 --> 01:24:18.644
Oh nothing.

01:24:19.376 --> 01:24:20.899
Eh? These guys again?

01:24:21.180 --> 01:24:23.587
Looks like they’ve come
with some new pickle today.

01:24:23.588 --> 01:24:25.162
- Sir...
- Oh, it’s you?

01:24:25.163 --> 01:24:26.944
Sir, Vineeth Sreenivasan’s been kidnapped!

01:24:26.945 --> 01:24:27.953
What?!

01:24:30.454 --> 01:24:31.516
WHAT?!

01:24:31.517 --> 01:24:33.977
Sir, he was supposed to sing
at our college.

01:24:33.978 --> 01:24:35.478
That guy kidnapped him.

01:24:35.479 --> 01:24:36.487
Which guy?

01:24:36.749 --> 01:24:38.576
That singing goon... Kuttan!

01:24:39.651 --> 01:24:42.150
How is that possible?
Vineeth Sreenivasan just called me.

01:24:42.151 --> 01:24:43.183
It’s true.

01:24:43.184 --> 01:24:45.157
I confirmed with cyber cell.

01:24:45.655 --> 01:24:46.687
But sir,

01:24:46.688 --> 01:24:49.454
I heard Vineeth Sreenivasan
is singing at Mamallassery Kavu today.

01:24:49.455 --> 01:24:50.832
What the hell?!
What about our Pro Show?!

01:24:50.833 --> 01:24:51.748
There?!

01:24:51.749 --> 01:24:53.717
Maybe you didn’t clear his payment.

01:24:54.064 --> 01:24:55.821
Why else would he take another gig?

01:24:55.822 --> 01:24:57.618
He’s not that kind of guy.
I know!

01:24:57.619 --> 01:25:00.172
Sir, please believe us,
Vineeth Sreenivasan is really kidnapped!

01:25:01.896 --> 01:25:03.538
That’s not possible.

01:25:04.407 --> 01:25:06.648
I’ll just call Vineeth Sreenivasan.

01:25:07.196 --> 01:25:08.751
Calling Vineeth Sreenivasan?

01:25:09.517 --> 01:25:10.549
Hello?

01:25:10.550 --> 01:25:11.870
Sir, I’m SI Manichan,

01:25:11.871 --> 01:25:14.003
the one you called earlier
to introduce yourself.

01:25:14.802 --> 01:25:16.207
The "top-class SI."

01:25:16.208 --> 01:25:17.215
Ah yes, yes.

01:25:17.596 --> 01:25:18.916
Sir, are you okay?

01:25:19.433 --> 01:25:20.829
I’m okay. I'm okay.

01:25:21.067 --> 01:25:23.864
Sir, are you singing
at Mamallassery Kavu tonight?

01:25:24.685 --> 01:25:26.679
Ye... yes, yes!

01:25:26.680 --> 01:25:29.018
So not performing at the college today?

01:25:30.470 --> 01:25:32.368
No, not at the college.

01:25:33.266 --> 01:25:35.532
Sir, you're not in any trouble, right?

01:25:35.533 --> 01:25:37.774
N... no trouble! No trouble at all.
I’m fine.

01:25:37.775 --> 01:25:40.078
May I know where you are, sir, now?

01:25:41.337 --> 01:25:42.658
Sir... I’m...

01:25:42.854 --> 01:25:45.034
at a very personal place right now.

01:25:48.715 --> 01:25:51.270
- Sorry sir, personal place? Okay, okay.
- Sir... sir...

01:25:51.368 --> 01:25:52.760
Sir, can we talk to him?

01:25:52.761 --> 01:25:54.729
Hey, he’s with family
at some personal place.

01:25:54.730 --> 01:25:57.191
Would any kidnapped guy pick up
on the first ring anyway?

01:25:57.192 --> 01:25:58.745
You guys and your wild stories!

01:25:58.746 --> 01:26:01.201
He clearly said
he’s performing elsewhere. Go!

01:26:01.202 --> 01:26:03.668
- Sir please, let us talk to him.
- Go! Go!

01:26:03.669 --> 01:26:05.646
- Can we just talk to him once?
- He's alright.

01:26:05.647 --> 01:26:08.365
- Sir, just once, please.
- You saw sir's level of reach, right?

01:26:08.366 --> 01:26:09.398
Get lost!

01:26:09.399 --> 01:26:10.911
We already settled payment, right?

01:26:10.912 --> 01:26:12.848
- We paid the money!
- Let me call the manager.

01:26:13.966 --> 01:26:15.372
Sir...

01:26:15.373 --> 01:26:17.607
Maybe we should just look into it once.

01:26:18.158 --> 01:26:19.658
Just casually.

01:26:20.037 --> 01:26:22.205
Yeah, just make a neutral inquiry.

01:26:22.922 --> 01:26:25.598
- Sir.
- ...calling up SI Manichan to the stage.

01:26:35.674 --> 01:26:39.509
♪ O, Mother, my warm blanket ♪

01:26:41.682 --> 01:26:43.620
♪ O, Mother, my warm blanket ♪

01:26:43.621 --> 01:26:48.126
♪ A thousand nights ahead,
wrapped in your warmth ♪

01:26:51.589 --> 01:26:53.315
Unbelievable, right?

01:26:54.540 --> 01:26:56.165
Did you figure out the raga?

01:26:58.586 --> 01:26:59.594
Bhimpalasi.

01:27:00.501 --> 01:27:02.360
Are you an absolute idiot, mister?

01:27:02.361 --> 01:27:03.407
What the hell?

01:27:03.408 --> 01:27:05.626
I have never seen
such a bunch of blockheads in my life!

01:27:05.627 --> 01:27:06.996
Mother blanket?! What the hell is it?!

01:27:06.997 --> 01:27:09.105
Stop your damn bloody show!

01:27:09.698 --> 01:27:11.158
You weren’t even in the plan.

01:27:11.159 --> 01:27:12.503
You're just a bonus track.

01:27:12.504 --> 01:27:13.839
Do you remember me?

01:27:14.804 --> 01:27:17.013
Back in early Star Singer days,

01:27:17.014 --> 01:27:19.950
I sang at the open selection
in Mannamoola Karayogam Hall.

01:27:20.587 --> 01:27:22.862
♪ Don’t sob in that sweet voice ♪

01:27:23.431 --> 01:27:27.071
♪ Don’t let your eyes fill with tears ♪

01:27:27.283 --> 01:27:28.562
In the next line...

01:27:28.673 --> 01:27:32.978
♪ Even when silent pain fills the air... ♪

01:27:33.227 --> 01:27:36.086
When I raised my hand to catch the pitch,
what did you ask?

01:27:36.289 --> 01:27:37.968
"Is a plane flying over your head?!"

01:27:37.969 --> 01:27:40.998
Honestly, that day I almost
threw a 'thotta' into your studio.

01:27:40.999 --> 01:27:42.538
Planned it for two days!

01:27:43.546 --> 01:27:44.929
Then I dropped it

01:27:45.119 --> 01:27:46.789
You are an artist, after all!
I let it go.

01:27:46.790 --> 01:27:48.704
Hey... hey... hey!

01:27:48.807 --> 01:27:50.702
There is a power
called Bhagavathi, the Goddess!

01:27:50.703 --> 01:27:53.468
That’s exactly why you circled around
and landed right in my lap. Okay?

01:27:53.556 --> 01:27:55.947
Tonight, I’m running a program here.

01:27:56.821 --> 01:27:58.579
On that stage,

01:27:58.580 --> 01:28:00.385
he will sing the song I just sang with me.

01:28:02.168 --> 01:28:03.880
Here, lyrics of “Mother blanket."

01:28:04.004 --> 01:28:05.590
And you will play the harmonium too.

01:28:05.591 --> 01:28:07.301
On stage, live. In front of everyone.

01:28:07.676 --> 01:28:09.191
After that, I will drop you both

01:28:09.192 --> 01:28:11.393
at the railway station or bus stand
wherever you want.

01:28:11.609 --> 01:28:13.368
See? It's a good temple.

01:28:13.369 --> 01:28:15.016
Even got five-star ratings on Google.

01:28:16.848 --> 01:28:17.856
Mr. Kuttan...

01:28:18.348 --> 01:28:20.864
I apologize for his lame joke.

01:28:20.997 --> 01:28:22.699
No! Why you saying sorry?

01:28:23.028 --> 01:28:24.301
It’s a good comedy!

01:28:24.437 --> 01:28:25.780
See, Mr. Kuttan,

01:28:25.781 --> 01:28:27.543
he charges ten lakhs for a show.

01:28:27.544 --> 01:28:28.826
- That’s a bit steep.
- Eh?!

01:28:28.827 --> 01:28:30.545
But do you have that cash?

01:28:30.546 --> 01:28:32.161
Hey hey, hey, where’s this going?

01:28:32.162 --> 01:28:34.091
Calm down! Stay in your lane!

01:28:35.408 --> 01:28:39.087
It’s an honor enough that
you get to share a stage with me.
